&lt;h2&gt;


Limits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model files, LoRAs and detector weights are not bundled; every JSON references files that must exist in your environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Third-party LoRAs keep their own licenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results depend on prompt, seed, sampler settings and the base model version.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What this is about.&lt;/strong&gt; A tool I built for designing kayak colors grew into a t-shirt designer, the T-lab, on five of my sites. They all sell through one shop now.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why.&lt;/strong&gt; Run several sites on one codebase and sooner or later something has two truths. This is how I got back to one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A kayak with sleeves
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rebel Kayaks has a page where you paint, or design as it were, a kayak in proper RAL colours for factory coating. Then it occurred to me that a t-shirt is just a kayak with sleeves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few sessions later the T-lab existed. You draw on a tee, pick a colour, pay at rugd.se, and a print shop prints it and posts it. I ordered one and it arrived, the right way up. As of this week it's also the only one ever ordered, which turned out to be excellent timing for tearing the plumbing apart. Because of course I didn't market it and of course I forgot to create a link for it on the site! Doing it now. Oh well :)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Five sites, five opinions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My opening message to the AI:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;"the setup and infra sucks. It is way too complicated for any tenant admin, except me, with your help, to set up."&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every site kept its own copy of the garment list, and every copy aged in its own way. Somebody forgot...maybe the rubber duck? One site was proudly offering a sports tee the shop no longer sold. You could design it lovingly and then not buy it. How does this happen, I hear you think? Ah, a quick idea, no particular plan for scaling. You know, make a POC and see if it flies. or in code lingo: &lt;em&gt;move fast and break things&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;"The rugd shop can be an active "gate" but there can only be one truth."&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The least trash wins
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The AI came back with three ways out. One T-lab for everyone, every site reading the shop live, or keeping the copies and syncing them harder. I asked for the one that "leaves the least trash in code".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So the shop now says out loud what it sells, and every site listens. When the shop drops a garment, it vanishes everywhere at once. A site keeps only its own taste: which garments to offer, which colours to hide. A festival site can sell one tee. A shop site can sell all of them.&lt;br&gt;
Why this complicated, you think? Glad you asked! It is the exact same layout as a franchise. Now you suddenly know why it's worth it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The robot took the boring jobs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Prices follow what printing really costs, plus a margin. Every night the shop checks its garments against the print shop and tidies up what changed. A cheeky 90% discount code now stops at what the shirt costs to make, instead of you paying people to wear your designs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It wasn't flawless. The nightly check did its job perfectly on the first night and told nobody, so for a morning I thought it had never run. Now it announces itself, like a cat that wants credit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then it shipped, one site at a time, because shipping everything at once has bitten me before. The old way of syncing went in the bin, and deleting things is my favourite kind of progress.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What happened, and how else it could be done
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Five sites each kept a copy of the truth. Now one shop holds it and the sites read it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Way&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Better at&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Costs&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One T-lab for every site&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Literally one copy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Every site loses its own look&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The shop pushes changes to each site&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Instant&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The shop has to know every site and chase the ones that are down&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Copies, synced now and then (what I had)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Works with the shop offline&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Two truths, and steps that get forgotten&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sites read the shop (chosen)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One truth, simple sites&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Each site leans on the shop; a cached copy covers short outages&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rule I'm keeping: if two places can disagree, they will. Make one of them a reader.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published at &lt;a href="https://idunworks.com/the-kayak-designer-learned-to-sell-t-shirts" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;idunworks.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


From a $40 HIV Shot to Walking Inside the Capsid: Why Structural Biology Needs Spatial ...
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From a $40 HIV Shot to Walking Inside the Capsid: Why Structural Biology Needs Spatial Computing  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This week the U.S. approved a generic version of lenacapavir—a long‑acting HIV prevention shot—with an Indian manufacturer pledging to supply low‑ and middle‑income countries at just $40 per year. That’s a remarkable milestone for global health equity. It’s also a testament to structural biology: lenacapavir is a first‑in‑class capsid inhibitor. Its mechanism? It binds the HIV‑1 capsid protein at the interface between hexamer subunits, stabilizing the lattice and blocking the nuclear entry and disassembly steps the virus needs to replicate.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For students, educators, and drug discovery scientists, that mechanism is usually encountered as a static ribbon diagram on a flat screen. A PDB entry (e.g., 7L5Z, 7L60). A publication figure. Maybe a PyMOL session if you have the time and compute.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What if you could step inside that capsid lattice at human scale?  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NexoPeek&lt;/strong&gt; makes that possible. The Meta Quest application turns the headset into an interactive, 3D molecular laboratory. Rather than examining biological macromolecules on flat 2D monitors, users can step inside, walk around, grab, scale, and physically interact with 3D protein structures, ligands, and nucleic acids at human scale using bare hands or VR controllers. The app ships with twelve narrated tours across six thematic pillars—from Biotech Basics and Foundations of Life (hemoglobin oxygen binding, ATP production) through Pathways &amp;amp; Interactions (glycolysis, trypsin), Medicines in Action (aspirin COX inhibition), Genetic Technologies (CRISPR‑Cas9, Central Dogma, Yamanaka factors), and Green Biotech (plastic‑degrading enzymes). Each tour is grounded in real Protein Data Bank structures, turning abstract cellular mechanisms into tangible, walk‑through experiences.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Under the hood the runtime is built on Unity 2022 LTS with the OpenXR 1.1 subsystem, targeting Quest 2, Quest Pro, and Quest 3. The rendering pipeline uses a custom URP‑based shader that streams Mol*‑generated geometry directly to the GPU, keeping the frame budget under 11 ms (≈90 FPS) on Quest 2 and under 8 ms on Quest Pro. Hand‑tracking latency sits at ~12 ms thanks to the Quest Interaction SDK’s low‑level hand‑pose buffer; controller input adds another 3 ms. All heavy lifting—structure parsing, symmetry expansion, electron‑density volume upload—runs on a background Job‑System thread pool, so the main thread stays free for UI and passthrough compositing.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For advanced research, the Professional PDB Viewer suite provides a connected scientific workstation. Smart Search &amp;amp; Database Routing queries RCSB PDB, UniProtKB, AlphaFold DB, SWISS‑MODEL, and PDBe via smart keyword cascades and UniProt gene synonym resolution, with automated model validation. Local data ingestion supports PDB, CIF, MOL2, GRO, XYZ, DX, TC, and XTC files, letting users overlay electrostatic field‑line maps, custom bond definitions, and electron‑density volumes. Publication‑quality graphics are achieved through six one‑tap &lt;strong&gt;Mol* Presets&lt;/strong&gt; derived from MolViewSpec concepts, supporting cartoon, ball‑and‑stick, spacefill CPK, molecular surface, B‑factor heat, and tube‑trace representations. A typical preset configuration looks like:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"preset"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"surface-bfactor"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"colorScheme"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"bfactor"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"surfaceOpacity"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"clipPlane"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"enabled"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"normal"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"distance"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Granular sequence and chain control lets you scroll per‑chain amino‑acid sequences, tap individual residue “pills” to project a 3D visual halo, pin custom atoms, or isolate specific chains. On‑board analytics include AI Pocket Prediction (cloud‑based PrankWeb/P2Rank or an offline TensorFlow‑Lite model that runs entirely on‑device), Structural Alignment via an integrated Foldseek pipeline to evaluate domain function conservation and drug‑swapping hypotheses, Ligand Inspector with PubChem integration to scan hetero‑compounds, evaluate hydrogen‑bond networks, and fetch 3D ligands, and a Distance Calculator that trigger‑picks two atoms in 3D space to report exact angstrom measurements. A Room‑View toggle floats 3D molecular structures into the user’s real physical room while keeping the wall menu operable—mixed‑reality passthrough that keeps the scientific workstation grounded in the user’s environment.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I still remember the first time I launched the capsid tour in my cramped campus office. The morning light slipped through the blinds as I slipped the Quest Pro over my eyes, the faint hum of the HVAC the only soundtrack. The HIV‑1 capsid (PDB 7L5Z) materialised at waist height, a geodesic lattice of hexamers and pentamers glowing in a soft cyan. I reached out—no controller, just my bare hand—and the hexamer under my fingertips pulsed, each subunit highlighted in amber. A narration whispered, “Lenacapavir locks this interface,” and a tiny ligand appeared, snapping into the cleft like a key.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My graduate student, Maya, peered over my shoulder, her coffee steaming. “Can we see the electrostatic map?” she asked. Two taps later the field‑line overlay bloomed, red‑blue ribbons tracing the charge landscape that guides the inhibitor. We walked around the capsid, crouching to peer into the central channel, then stepping back to watch the whole assembly rotate. The Room‑View toggle kept the lab bench visible—my notebook, a half‑eaten bagel, the whiteboard scrawled with kinetic equations—so the molecule never felt like a detached hologram.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Later that week I used the same session in a 30‑minute undergraduate lecture. The students, seated in a semicircle, each donned a Quest 2. I guided them through the same tour, but now the narration paused at each subunit, letting them “grab” a hexamer and feel the resistance of the stabilized lattice. One student, Jorge, whispered, “I finally get why the drug stops the virus from uncoating.” His eyes widened when the distance calculator showed a 3.2 Å hydrogen bond between the inhibitor carbonyl and a conserved asparagine—numbers he’d only ever seen in a table.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The experience turned abstract concepts into tactile moments—something a flat screen never could. The mixed‑reality Room View kept the classroom grounded; the professional viewer let me pull up the same structure later, run a Foldseek alignment against a bacterial capsid, and export a Mol* preset for a manuscript figure—all without leaving the headset.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you teach, research, or simply wonder how a $40 shot can block a virus at the molecular level, NexoPeek offers a hands‑on gateway that respects the science and the scientist. It is not a medical device; it is a visualisation platform that empowers better‑informed decisions.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.meta.com/experiences/nexopeek/1453797551140347/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://www.meta.com/experiences/nexopeek/1453797551140347/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I've been developing software for over 25 years. I've worked with old COBOL systems, modern web applications, financial platforms, and pretty much every generation of technology in between.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And there's something that has always bothered me.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why the hell are we still rewriting the same financial rules?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every time someone starts a new fintech, ERP, banking application, or financial SaaS, the story repeats itself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How should we round money? What happens when two operations modify the same financial record? Can an approval become invalid? What should happen when a transaction fails halfway through? How do we preserve audit evidence?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Different companies. Different architectures. Different programming languages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Same fundamental questions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And somehow, we keep answering them from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


So I started digging.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I went back to old books, financial systems, legacy implementations, regulations, and years of experience working with financial software.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looking for the rules that should never have been reinvented in the first place.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What I found wasn't a shortage of solutions. It was a shortage of shared, precise, verifiable foundations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We have countless libraries, frameworks, platforms, and architectures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But how often do we agree on what the correct financial behavior should actually be?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's where FinKore started.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Meet FinKore.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://finkore.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;FinKore&lt;/a&gt; is an open-source initiative to define a common foundation for financial software.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's not another framework or SaaS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's not an Lib you install and magically solve your financial problems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FinKore is about defining the rules before writing the code.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The idea is simple: fundamental financial behavior should be documented, explicit, testable, and independent of programming languages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your application might be written in TypeScript, Java, Go, or something that hasn't even been invented yet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The underlying financial rules shouldn't change just because your technology does.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


So Rules first. Code after.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FinKore is organized around three fundamental layers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CoreDoc -&amp;gt; Specifications -&amp;gt; Conformance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CoreDoc&lt;/strong&gt; establishes the financial principles and obligations. This is where we explain &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; a rule exists.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specifications&lt;/strong&gt; translate those principles into precise technical requirements, defining expected behavior, constraints, and failure conditions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conformance&lt;/strong&gt; provides portable test cases with inputs and expected results, allowing implementations to be evaluated against the same requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's the idea behind FinKore.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not to tell you which framework to use, but to establish what behavior your implementation should guarantee.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Five domains. One shared foundation.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FinKore currently focuses on five foundational domains:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Money:&lt;/strong&gt; Exact calculations, currency, rounding, allocation, and serialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Workflow:&lt;/strong&gt; Valid state transitions, lifecycle behavior, and rejection rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Audit:&lt;/strong&gt; Preserving evidence of what happened, who acted, and what must remain traceable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Approvals:&lt;/strong&gt; Decisions, conditions, approval validity, and the facts behind authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Financial Entities:&lt;/strong&gt; Identity, validation, revisions, and controlled changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are not complete banking products or accounting systems. They are building blocks that financial applications can use to establish predictable behavior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And importantly, FinKore doesn't decide your business policies for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It defines the foundation. Your application defines its own business rules, architecture, and integrations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What about AI?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If an AI doesn't know which rounding policy applies, when an approval expires, or how an operation must behave after rejection, it will make assumptions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And assumptions are dangerous in financial software.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FinKore provides explicit specifications and machine-readable operation contracts that can help developers and AI-assisted workflows work from defined expectations instead of inventing behavior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI should implement financial rules, not invent them.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


I'm not trying to build this alone.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is probably the most important part.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I don't believe one developer, one company, or even one engineering team has all the answers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A developer understands implementation constraints. An accountant understands financial obligations. An auditor understands evidence and controls. A financial architect understands how these requirements interact across systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FinKore needs all of these perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's why the project is open-source and community-driven.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I want people to challenge the specifications, find missing scenarios, question assumptions, propose edge cases, and help make the foundation stronger.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You don't need to contribute code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes a difficult question from an auditor is more valuable than a thousand lines of implementation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


We're just getting started.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FinKore already has published specifications, portable conformance cases, documentation, and a growing set of discussions about financial behavior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But I see this as the beginning, not the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I want FinKore to become a shared reference that developers can rely on when building financial products, regardless of the technology they choose.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not because everyone should write the same code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But because we shouldn't have to reinvent the same financial foundations forever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your product may be unique. Your financial rules don't have to be.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you've worked with financial software, I'd love to hear what rules you've had to implement over and over again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And if you disagree with something in FinKore, even better. Open a discussion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's how we improve it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explore the project:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://finkore.dev" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://finkore.dev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/willgittens/FinKore" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/willgittens/FinKore&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Define once. Build many times.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published at &lt;a href="https://aicoding-guide.com/en/posts/weekly-2026-11-08/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://aicoding-guide.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The change with the widest reach this week is that &lt;strong&gt;auto mode no longer falls back to the built-in classifier&lt;/strong&gt;. Where telemetry or feature flags are off, including behind an LLM gateway, calls the server cannot check are &lt;strong&gt;asked about or denied&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For unattended runs, &lt;code&gt;permissions.denyInsteadOfPrompting&lt;/code&gt; is new: instead of stalling on a prompt, the call is denied and the turn continues.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key point&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
This week in brief&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Auto mode asks about or denies calls the server can't check, with no classifier fallback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;permissions.denyInsteadOfPrompting&lt;/code&gt; replaces a stalled prompt with a denial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web and shell tool calls now ask before sending your account email address&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Claude Code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Three releases: 2.1.317, 2.1.318 and 2.1.319.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Auto mode lost its fallback (2.1.319)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The CHANGELOG reads: "Changed auto mode with telemetry or feature flags off, including behind LLM gateways: calls the server can't check are asked about or denied, with no fallback to the built-in classifier; set &lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_MODE_SERVER=0&lt;/code&gt; to keep using it (Bedrock, Vertex and Foundry are unchanged)."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Environment&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Effect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Telemetry or feature flags off&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Calls the server can't check are asked about or denied&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Behind an LLM gateway&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The same&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Bedrock / Vertex / Foundry&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Unchanged&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_MODE_SERVER=0&lt;/code&gt; restores the previous behaviour of using the built-in classifier. In the other direction, &lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_MODE_SERVER=1&lt;/code&gt; turns the server-side check on behind a gateway even with &lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS&lt;/code&gt; set — and where managed settings set the latter, they must set the &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt; too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Relatedly, &lt;code&gt;/status&lt;/code&gt; no longer reports "Auto mode server: Enabled" when the server-side review is not actually reaching the session. For how the modes differ, see &lt;a href="https://aicoding-guide.com/en/posts/claude-code-default-mode/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Claude Code starts in auto mode by default&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


New settings and variables (2.1.319)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;permissions.denyInsteadOfPrompting&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Denies a call that would wait on a permission prompt and continues the turn, in terminal sessions, subagents and teammates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_FEATURE_FLAGS&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stops feature-flag fetching without turning telemetry off; every flag uses its built-in default&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_MCP_TASK_BACKGROUND&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Waits for an MCP task inside its tool call instead of backgrounding it immediately&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MCP tasks are now supported in the terminal: when a server runs a tool call as a task, Claude Code moves it to the background right away and reports the result when it finishes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disabling feature flags also stops idle compaction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_FEATURE_FLAGS&lt;/code&gt; stops flag fetching while leaving telemetry on. One of idle compaction's conditions is that Claude Code can fetch feature flags from Anthropic, so setting this variable stops it running. For the full list of conditions, see &lt;a href="https://aicoding-guide.com/en/posts/claude-code-autocompact-window/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Making Claude Code compact earlier, or never&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


A check before your email address goes out (2.1.317)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;New in 2.1.317: "Added a check that asks before a web or shell tool call sends your account email address to the network."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Three security fixes also landed:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;code&gt;sed&lt;/code&gt; command could skip the permission check in accept-edits and auto mode (2.1.319)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bash deny and ask rules missed commands written with quoted words (2.1.319)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;/rewind&lt;/code&gt; could restore or delete a file through a directory symlink (2.1.319)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Sign-in expiry is now visible (2.1.318)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This one matters for unattended runs. The expiry date of a stored claude.ai sign-in is now available as &lt;code&gt;loginExpiresAt&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;claude auth status&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;credential_expires_at&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;claude -p&lt;/code&gt; JSON results, with a one-line stderr warning starting 10 days before.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The release itself is mostly fixes for configuration files and stored logins being corrupted on network home directories, so it is worth taking if you run on a shared home. Claude Code also no longer installs or updates the IDE extension when started from an IDE terminal; use &lt;code&gt;/ide&lt;/code&gt; from an outside terminal instead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Codex
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;v0.167.0 ships six features.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Addition&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;codex agents --no-daemon&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Opens the agent command center; it and the session picker now mark unread results&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Backend switching&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Switch between connected backends from the terminal session picker, keeping drafts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Image preview&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Preview local image attachments while composing, on supported terminals&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;gcp_setup_wizard&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Sets up Google Cloud Vertex AI with Application Default Credentials or a credential file&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;System proxy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Opt into macOS or Windows system proxy settings from &lt;code&gt;/experimental&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Patch details&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Expand patch details in the transcript while an approval prompt is open&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;gcp_setup_wizard&lt;/code&gt; continues from v0.165.0, which made Vertex AI a built-in provider via &lt;code&gt;model_provider = "gcp"&lt;/code&gt; — see &lt;a href="https://aicoding-guide.com/en/posts/codex-update-0-165/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Codex CLI v0.165 makes Vertex AI a built-in provider&lt;/a&gt;. The API key and cloud provider options moved under the "Sign in another way" menu.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Three fixes stand out. Saved chats stay visible after switching model providers, and a chat that cannot resume can still be read and turned into an editable prompt for a new chat. Network approval prompts close when their requests end, and concurrent requests to the same endpoint prompt one at a time. Automatic context compaction now accounts for retained output from failed responses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Gemini CLI
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;v0.67.0 (November 4) has two features among 27 entries: the &lt;code&gt;models&lt;/code&gt; command, and the fix for a Claude hook timeout that migrated 1000x too small. See &lt;a href="https://aicoding-guide.com/en/posts/gemini-cli-update-0-67/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Gemini CLI v0.67 adds a models command and fixes the unit in Claude hook migration&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What to check now
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you run auto mode behind an LLM gateway, note the 2.1.319 change and set &lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_MODE_SERVER&lt;/code&gt; if needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For unattended runs that must not stall, consider &lt;code&gt;permissions.denyInsteadOfPrompting&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check your sign-in expiry with &lt;code&gt;claude auth status&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move to 2.1.318 if you run on a network home directory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Auto mode asks about or denies calls the server can't check, with no classifier fallback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_MODE_SERVER=0&lt;/code&gt; restores the old behaviour; Bedrock, Vertex and Foundry are unchanged&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;permissions.denyInsteadOfPrompting&lt;/code&gt; turns a stalled prompt into a denial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web and shell tool calls ask before sending your account email address&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Codex 0.167.0 adds &lt;code&gt;gcp_setup_wizard&lt;/code&gt; and opt-in system proxy settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fcxo3ondcztv407rewkvl.webp" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fcxo3ondcztv407rewkvl.webp" alt="&amp;quot;A Lightweight Real-Time Notification System with FastAPI, Redis Pub/Sub, SSE, and React Query&amp;quot;&lt;br&gt;
" width="748" height="424"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


A Lightweight Real-Time Notification System with FastAPI, Redis Pub/Sub, SSE, and React Query
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A useful notification feature needs to do two things well:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a durable history users can return to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show new activity quickly without asking users to refresh the page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Those are related problems, but they are not the same problem. A database is a good source of truth for notification history. A live connection is useful for timely updates. For a small application, PostgreSQL, Redis Pub/Sub, Server-Sent Events (SSE), and TanStack Query can cover both without introducing a separate broker and worker fleet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This post walks through that design using a FastAPI backend and a React/Next.js frontend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope:&lt;/strong&gt; this is a lightweight, best-effort real-time design. It does not promise exactly-once delivery or replay of every event. The database is durable; Redis Pub/Sub is not.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Architecture
&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Business operation
│
▼
Notification service
├── Insert notification into PostgreSQL
└── Publish a live event to Redis Pub/Sub
│
▼
FastAPI SSE endpoint
│
▼
Browser EventSource
│
▼
TanStack Query cache / UI

Notification history and unread count ──► PostgreSQL
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The distinction is important:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;PostgreSQL&lt;/strong&gt; stores notification history and read/archive state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Redis Pub/Sub&lt;/strong&gt; broadcasts updates to clients listening right now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SSE&lt;/strong&gt; keeps a server-to-browser connection open over HTTP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;TanStack Query&lt;/strong&gt; handles history, unread counts, and cache updates in the UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If a browser is offline or disconnects, it can fetch the durable notification list when it reconnects. It cannot replay missed Redis Pub/Sub messages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Backend: persist notifications as domain data
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


1. Model and schema
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each notification belongs to a user and an organization. That scope should be applied consistently to reads, updates, deletes, and live channels.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Base&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUIDPrimaryKeyMixin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;TenantMixin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;TimestampMixin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;__tablename__&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ForeignKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;auth_user.id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ondelete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;CASCADE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;nullable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;index&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;255&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nullable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nullable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;action_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;dict&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;JSONB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nullable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;server_default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_archived&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Mapped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;mapped_column&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;nullable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;server_default&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;meta&lt;/code&gt; is for optional, structured context such as a &lt;code&gt;trip_id&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;expense_id&lt;/code&gt;. Keep it as JSON data; do not treat it as trusted HTML.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Pydantic response schema should expose the same identifier and fields in both ordinary API responses and live events:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NotificationResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseModel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;model_config&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ConfigDict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;from_attributes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nb"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;action_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;dict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_archived&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;created_at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;datetime&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In the deployed model, the primary key is a UUID named &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;. The frontend must use that identifier; it should not assume a numeric &lt;code&gt;pkid&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An Alembic migration creates the table, foreign keys, and indexes. Indexes on &lt;code&gt;(user_id, is_read)&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;(user_id, is_archived)&lt;/code&gt; help the common unread and archive filters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Keep database access in the repository
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The repository owns SQLAlchemy queries. Every user-facing query includes both &lt;code&gt;user_id&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;organization_id&lt;/code&gt;; this prevents an ID from another tenant from being used to read or mutate a notification.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;list_query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;unread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;is_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_archived&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;is_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;elif&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;archive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_archived&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;is_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_archived&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;is_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;order_by&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;created_at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;desc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Unread counts should use the same definition as the unread list:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;stmt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;func&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;is_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_archived&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;is_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Cursor pagination keeps list requests small as notification history grows. The FastAPI route uses &lt;code&gt;CursorPage&lt;/code&gt;; the frontend should read its &lt;code&gt;next_page&lt;/code&gt; field to request the next page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Create notifications from domain services
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Business services know when an event matters. They call the notification service rather than coupling domain logic to Redis channel names or serialization.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;notification_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create_notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;NotificationCreate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;trip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;created_by_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Trip allocated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Trip &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;trip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;transaction_number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; was allocated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;NotificationCategory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;TRIPS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;trip_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;trip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The notification service persists via the repository and then publishes a JSON-safe representation:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;notification&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;repo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;event_data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;NotificationResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;model_validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;from_attributes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;model_dump&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;mode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;publish_notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;event_type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;**&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event_data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The attached implementation publishes during the request while the request-scoped database session is still open. The repository flushes the insert, and the request dependency commits later. This means Redis can deliver an event before the database transaction commits. An immediate history refetch can race that commit, too. For a small system, refetch with a small delay/retry or accept eventual UI refresh; do not claim that the event and database commit are atomic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For stronger consistency, write an &lt;strong&gt;outbox row in the same transaction&lt;/strong&gt; as the notification. A worker can publish committed outbox records and retry failures. That is a reliability upgrade, not a feature Redis Pub/Sub provides by itself.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Publish and subscribe on user-scoped channels
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use organization and user IDs in channel names:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;notifications:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;publish&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dumps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event_data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Unread-count changes can use a separate channel:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;notifications:count:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;publish&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dumps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Do not let clients choose these IDs. Derive the user and active organization from the authenticated request, and only subscribe the server-side stream to those values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Encode real SSE events correctly
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SSE has a wire format with named events, data, and optional comments. With &lt;code&gt;sse-starlette&lt;/code&gt;, yield &lt;code&gt;ServerSentEvent&lt;/code&gt; objects (or supported event dictionaries), not strings that already contain &lt;code&gt;event:&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; lines. A plain string is encoded as an SSE &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; value; wrapping preformatted SSE text as a string does not preserve it as event framing.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;redis.asyncio&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Redis&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sse_starlette.sse&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ServerSentEvent&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;notification_stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;UUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;initial_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;notifications:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;pubsub&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;pubsub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pubsub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;subscribe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;yield&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ServerSentEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dumps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;initial_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;wait_for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;pubsub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get_message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ignore_subscribe_messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;timeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;except&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TimeoutError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;yield&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ServerSentEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;heartbeat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;continue&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;loads&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;event_name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;pop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;event_type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;yield&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ServerSentEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;event_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dumps&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pubsub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;unsubscribe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pubsub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;aclose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The timeout is handled inside the loop so heartbeats continue while the stream is idle. Also retain cancellation handling and cleanup; an SSE connection can live much longer than an ordinary request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The route returns the stream using &lt;code&gt;EventSourceResponse&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ActiveMemberDep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Annotated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;OrganizationMember&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Depends&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;resolve_active_member&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;CurrentUserDep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Annotated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;UserResponseSchema&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Depends&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;get_current_active_user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;DbSessionDep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Annotated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;AsyncSession&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Depends&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;get_db_session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;scope&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;RedisDep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Annotated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Depends&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;get_redis_from_request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)]&lt;/span&gt;


&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@router.get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;/stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;stream_notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;member&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ActiveMemberDep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;current_user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;CurrentUserDep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;DbSessionDep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;RedisDep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;initial_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;notification_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get_unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;current_user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;member&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;events&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;notification_stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;current_user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;member&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;initial_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EventSourceResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Authentication and active-membership resolution happen before returning the stream. The stream’s Redis subscription is then scoped to that authenticated user and organization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


6. Expose history and state-changing endpoints
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A small API usually needs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Method&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Path&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Purpose&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/notifications?tab=all&amp;amp;size=10&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cursor-paginated history&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/notifications/unread-count&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Current unread count&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/notifications/stream&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Named SSE events&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;PATCH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/notifications/{id}/read&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mark one as read&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;PATCH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/notifications/mark-all-read&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mark visible unread notifications as read&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;PATCH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/notifications/{id}/archive&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Archive one notification&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;DELETE&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;/v1/notifications/{id}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Delete one notification&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use UUID path parameters in the backend. In the example application, the notification router is mounted under &lt;code&gt;/query/api/v1/notifications&lt;/code&gt;; the frontend reaches the upstream service through its &lt;code&gt;/api&lt;/code&gt; Next.js proxy. Confirm your deployment’s proxy/base URL instead of copying a path without checking it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Frontend: make the API contract explicit
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The attached frontend types and component use &lt;code&gt;pkid: number&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;next_cursor&lt;/code&gt;, and category names such as &lt;code&gt;BOOKING&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;SCHEDULING&lt;/code&gt;. The backend returns &lt;code&gt;id: UUID&lt;/code&gt;, cursor-page fields including &lt;code&gt;next_page&lt;/code&gt;, and categories such as &lt;code&gt;TRIPS&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;EXPENSES&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;PAYMENTS&lt;/code&gt;. These contracts need to match or be translated at one explicit boundary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the API shown above, define the frontend types from the backend contract:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationCategory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;SYSTEM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;COMMUNICATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;ADMINISTRATIVE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;PAYMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;EXPENSES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;TRIPS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationTab&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;unread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;archive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// UUID serialized as a string&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;organization_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;user_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationCategory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;action_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Record&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;is_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;is_archived&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;created_at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationPage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;next_page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;previous_page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; consistently for React keys, mutation variables, cache matching, and API routes. If an older frontend needs a numeric &lt;code&gt;pkid&lt;/code&gt;, build and test an adapter; do not silently assume the backend UUID can be used as a number.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Query history and unread count
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The frontend API functions call the durable endpoints. &lt;code&gt;getNextPageParam&lt;/code&gt; must match the backend cursor response:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useInfiniteNotifications&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationTab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationCategory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useInfiniteQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;initialPageParam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;queryFn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pageParam&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/v1/notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;cursor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pageParam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;getNextPageParam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lastPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;next_page&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The unread count is a separate query so the badge can be updated independently:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useNotificationUnreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;unread-count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;queryFn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/v1/notifications/unread-count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;staleTime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;retry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The current Next.js fetcher sends requests to a same-origin &lt;code&gt;/api/...&lt;/code&gt; route, which forwards cookies upstream. Use that same origin for SSE when possible:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EventSource&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/api/v1/notifications/stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;withCredentials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This avoids hard-coding a backend host in a client component. For direct cross-origin SSE, configure CORS and cookie attributes deliberately, and use the correct upstream base path (the backend router is mounted beneath &lt;code&gt;/query/api&lt;/code&gt; in this application).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Listen for named events—not only &lt;code&gt;onmessage&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The backend sends named SSE events: &lt;code&gt;connected&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;notification&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;unread_count&lt;/code&gt;. Browser &lt;code&gt;EventSource.onmessage&lt;/code&gt; handles only unnamed &lt;code&gt;message&lt;/code&gt; events. Register listeners for each custom event:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;EventSource&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/api/v1/notifications/stream&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;withCredentials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;MessageEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQueryData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UnreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;200&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onNotification&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;_event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// History is durable; refetch it instead of trusting a transient event&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// to maintain cursor pages and every active tab/category filter.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;invalidateQueries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;invalidateQueries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onUnreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;MessageEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQueryData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UnreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;200&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onNotification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onUnreadCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;onerror&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// EventSource retries automatically unless the connection is closed.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Keep the durable list endpoint as the recovery path.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onNotification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onUnreadCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;close&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The important correction is &lt;code&gt;addEventListener&lt;/code&gt;. If the server sets &lt;code&gt;event: notification&lt;/code&gt;, that event will not arrive through &lt;code&gt;source.onmessage&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Invalidating the list on a notification event is intentionally conservative. Prepending into every cached cursor page can put items into the wrong tab, category, or page. If you choose to update the cache directly for a snappier UI, deduplicate by &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; and update only query keys whose filters match the event.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Make read/archive/delete actions optimistic
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TanStack Query mutations can update the UI before the server responds. The safe pattern is:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cancel queries that could overwrite the optimistic change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snapshot the affected caches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply the change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Restore the snapshots if the mutation fails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invalidate the queries after settlement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, mark-read mutations should accept the backend UUID:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;InfiniteData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;QueryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMutation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;useQueryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@tanstack/react-query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ApiError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;patch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/lib/fetcher&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UnreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;unread-count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationMutationContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;lists&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Array&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;QueryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;InfiniteData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;unreadCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UnreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;markRead&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;patch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/v1/notifications/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/read`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMarkNotificationRead&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useQueryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMutation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ApiError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationMutationContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;mutationFn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;markRead&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onMutate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;cancelQueries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;cancelQueries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lists&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;getQueriesData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;InfiniteData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;getQueryData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UnreadCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lists&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;flatMap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(([,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;flatMap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;find&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Snapshot first. Then update matching items by their UUID.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lists&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;continue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationTab&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQueryData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;InfiniteData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NotificationPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;pages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tab&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;unread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;is_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;is_read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQueryData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UnreadCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unread_count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;old&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lists&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unreadCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;lists&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;forEach&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQueryData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unreadCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQueryData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unreadCount&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onSettled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;invalidateQueries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;notifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;queryClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;invalidateQueries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;queryKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;UNREAD_COUNT_QUERY_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For a real implementation, decrement the cached unread count only when the target item was unread, and remove it from an unread-only list. The attached mutation hooks already use this snapshot/rollback pattern; the key contract correction is changing their identifier from numeric &lt;code&gt;pkid&lt;/code&gt; to string &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Archiving marks a notification as read in the backend. Ensure the unread count is updated for other connected clients too: publish a fresh count after archive, or have the client invalidate/refetch its count. The backend should be the source of truth for that count.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where background tasks fit
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Despite the common “background task” framing, this implementation does not use FastAPI &lt;code&gt;BackgroundTasks&lt;/code&gt; for notification delivery. It stores a notification and publishes the Redis message during the request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is deliberate for a simple first version: the notification record is part of the application workflow, and the live publish is a small operation. FastAPI background tasks run in the API process after the response; they are not a durable queue. A process restart can lose pending work, and sharing a request-scoped SQLAlchemy session with a task is unsafe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If email, push delivery, retries, or high-volume fan-out become requirements, use a durable worker pattern. A transactional outbox is a practical next step:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Save the notification and an outbox event in one database transaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A worker claims undelivered outbox rows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The worker publishes and retries failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mark events delivered idempotently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use a task queue when you need durable execution, controlled concurrency, retries, or scheduling—not just because a task happens after a request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Operational and security checklist
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derive the user and organization from authenticated dependencies, not request payloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope every notification query and mutation by notification ID, user ID, and organization ID.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep Redis channels user- and organization-specific.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate category values and bound cursor page sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat Redis delivery as best effort; retrieve durable history from PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close Redis Pub/Sub subscriptions when clients disconnect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Send heartbeats and configure reverse proxies not to buffer the SSE response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Avoid logging notification bodies or sensitive metadata.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set CORS and cookie settings deliberately for cross-origin EventSource connections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor Redis connection health; application startup may succeed in degraded mode, but live delivery will not be available until Redis recovers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For reliable publishing after database commit, use an outbox rather than assuming a database flush is a commit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Integration gaps to close before calling the attached code end-to-end
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The backend and frontend snippets show the intended architecture, but the attached files currently have contract differences worth fixing:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SSE framing:&lt;/strong&gt; the backend generator yields preformatted strings and passes them to &lt;code&gt;EventSourceResponse&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;sse-starlette&lt;/code&gt; encodes ordinary strings as &lt;code&gt;data:&lt;/code&gt; values. Yield &lt;code&gt;ServerSentEvent&lt;/code&gt; objects or event dictionaries for custom event names.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Named SSE handlers:&lt;/strong&gt; the frontend uses &lt;code&gt;source.onmessage&lt;/code&gt;, while the backend names events. Use &lt;code&gt;addEventListener("notification", ...)&lt;/code&gt; and the matching listeners for &lt;code&gt;connected&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;unread_count&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Identifiers:&lt;/strong&gt; the backend exposes UUID &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;; the frontend types and mutations use numeric &lt;code&gt;pkid&lt;/code&gt;. Use the UUID string consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cursor fields:&lt;/strong&gt; the backend cursor page exposes &lt;code&gt;next_page&lt;/code&gt;; the frontend query currently reads &lt;code&gt;next_cursor&lt;/code&gt;. Read the actual &lt;code&gt;CursorPage&lt;/code&gt; field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Categories:&lt;/strong&gt; align frontend category unions and UI labels with the backend values (&lt;code&gt;SYSTEM&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;COMMUNICATION&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ADMINISTRATIVE&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PAYMENTS&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;EXPENSES&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;TRIPS&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unread count after archive:&lt;/strong&gt; archiving marks the record read, so also publish the updated count or refetch it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Transaction ordering:&lt;/strong&gt; Redis publication currently occurs before the request-scoped database transaction commits. Treat the event as a hint and refetch, or add a transactional outbox for reliable ordering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are not reasons to abandon the design. They are exactly the sorts of details an explicit end-to-end contract makes easier to spot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Closing
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A small notification system can be built from familiar pieces: store user-visible history in PostgreSQL, publish live hints through Redis Pub/Sub, stream them with SSE, and let TanStack Query manage the browser cache.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The simple design works best when its guarantees are stated honestly. Redis Pub/Sub is not durable, SSE is one-way, and a live event should not replace the history API. Align the event names, IDs, pagination fields, and categories across the backend and frontend; then add an outbox or worker only when delivery requirements justify the extra machinery.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En una interfaz de registro o verificación, el estado de correo no es un detalle del backend. Es una parte visible del producto: la persona pulsa un botón, espera una respuesta y necesita saber si puede continuar. Cuando ese estado aparece tarde, mueve el formulario o bloquea toda la pantalla, una operación correcta se siente rota.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Este patrón me ha resultado util en flujos de React que prueban el envío de correo, incluso cuando se usa un fake email generator para crear datos de prueba. La meta no es hacer que cada cambio sea espectacular, sino que sea predecible, accesible y barato para el navegador.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


El problema no es solo esperar
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un botón de “Enviar código” suele tener al menos cuatro estados: disponible, enviando, enviado y error. El problema aparece cuando la interfaz trata esos estados como una sola cosa. Por ejemplo, deshabilitar todo el formulario mientras llega la respuesta puede evitar un doble envío, pero tambien impide corregir otro campo o consultar una instrucción.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Antes de escribir JSX, anoto estas preguntas:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿Qué control conserva el foco durante la espera?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿Qué parte de la pantalla cambia y cuanto espacio necesita?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿Cómo se anuncia el resultado a un lector de pantalla?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿Qué ocurre si la respuesta llega despues de otra acción?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Una revisión relacionada es la de estos &lt;a href="https://dev.to/silviutech/react-estados-async-sin-saltos-visuales-22g3"&gt;estados async sin saltos visuales&lt;/a&gt;. La idea central es la misma: el cambio de estado debe tener un lugar estable y una causa visible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Diseñar un contrato de estados
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para un formulario pequeño prefiero un estado explícito en vez de varios booleanos que pueden contradecirse. &lt;code&gt;idle&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;loading&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;success&lt;/code&gt; y &lt;code&gt;error&lt;/code&gt; forman un contrato sencillo. Cada estado define qué puede hacer la persona y qué mensaje debe ver.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un detalle importante es separar el estado de red del estado de edición. Mientras se envía el correo, el botón puede estar deshabilitado, pero los campos no tienen por qué desaparecer ni quedar bloqueados. Si el servidor responde con error, el mensaje debe explicar el siguiente paso, no solo decir “fallo”.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;También conviene guardar un identificador de operación. Si alguien pulsa dos veces en una secuencia rápida y la primera respuesta llega al final, no deberia sobrescribir el resultado más reciente. No hace falta una arquitectura enorme: una variable de versión o un &lt;code&gt;AbortController&lt;/code&gt; puede proteger ese borde.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Un componente pequeño en React
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Este ejemplo mantiene el foco en el botón durante la espera y reserva un mensaje para el resultado. El &lt;code&gt;aria-live&lt;/code&gt; anuncia el cambio sin obligar a mover el cursor de forma inesperada.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;EmailCodeForm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sendCode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;preventDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;++&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendCode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;requestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Enviando el código…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Código enviado. Revisa tu bandeja.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;No pudimos enviarlo. Revisa el dato e inténtalo de nuevo.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-busy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;htmlFor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Correo&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;disabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Enviando…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Enviar código&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"form-message"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"polite"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;El ejemplo no valida el correo en el cliente porque esa decisión depende del producto. Sí muestra dos límites útiles: el botón evita un envío accidental durante la espera y una respuesta vieja no reemplaza el estado actual. En una aplicación real, &lt;code&gt;sendCode&lt;/code&gt; debe recibir los datos del formulario y manejar sus errores con una forma consistente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


CSS que reserva espacio
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;El mensaje vacío sigue ocupando espacio. Así se evita que el botón salte cuando aparece la respuesta, y el usuario conserva una referencia visual estable.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.form-message&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;min-height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;1.5rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;margin-block&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0.5rem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;:focus-visible&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;:focus-visible&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;outline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;3px&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;solid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#155eef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;outline-offset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;3px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@media&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;prefers-reduced-motion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;scroll-behavior&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;auto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;transition-duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0.01ms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No usaría una animación para esconder una latencia que el producto no ha resuelto. Una transición corta puede ayudar, pero el mensaje debe aparecer rapido y sin cambiar el alto de varios bloques. Si el flujo tiene información operativa, un enlace contextual como &lt;a href="https://dev.to/alexcarteruk/terraform-correos-de-drift-que-si-orientan-211j"&gt;correos de drift que sí orientan&lt;/a&gt; puede aportar contexto, siempre que no compita con la acción principal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Probar con teclado y una red lenta
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La prueba más barata es recorrer el flujo solo con teclado: enfocar el campo, enviar, esperar, provocar un error y volver a intentarlo. El foco debe seguir siendo visible en cada paso. El mensaje no deberia ser la única señal; el botón, el texto y el estado de carga tienen que contar una historia coherente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Después simulo una red lenta y dos respuestas fuera de orden. Reviso que:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;el formulario no cambie de tamaño al mostrar el resultado;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;el lector de pantalla reciba el mensaje una sola vez;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;el botón vuelva a estar disponible tras un error;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;el segundo intento no sea reemplazado por la respuesta antigua;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;el campo conserve su valor cuando eso ayude a corregirlo;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;el foco no salte al principio de la página sin motivo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Durante las pruebas, una búsqueda como “tem email” puede aparecer en datos introducidos por usuarios. Es una etiqueta con error, no un nombre que debamos convertir en una variable o en un enlace. Del mismo modo, si se usa un &lt;a href="https://tempmailso.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;generar correo desechable&lt;/a&gt; para un escenario de QA, el flujo de prueba debe comprobar el estado de la interfaz, no solamente que llegó un mensaje.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Preguntas rápidas
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Debo deshabilitar todo el formulario mientras envío?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No siempre. Deshabilita la acción que podría duplicarse y conserva editables los campos si la persona puede corregirlos sin invalidar la petición en curso. Elige el límite según el contrato del backend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Es mejor mover el foco al mensaje de éxito?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Solo cuando el resultado sea el siguiente paso esencial. Para una confirmación breve, &lt;code&gt;aria-live="polite"&lt;/code&gt; suele ser suficiente y deja que la persona siga en su contexto.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


¿Cómo mido si la interfaz mejoró?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mide el tiempo desde la acción hasta el primer feedback, los errores de doble envío y los abandonos durante la espera. No persigas una cifra aislada: una respuesta mas rapida que no explica el resultado sigue siendo una mala experiencia.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Los estados de correo bien diseñados conectan React, CSS y accesibilidad sin pedir una infraestructura complicada. Un contrato claro, espacio reservado y una prueba con respuestas lentas suelen revelar mas problemas que otra capa de animación.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built a booking app for gyms with React, TanStack Start and Supabase. The part that looked easy and wasn't: two people booking the same slot at the same moment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This post explains the approach I ended up with, with a simplified version of the code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The problem&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A client opens the booking page, picks a service, a date and a time slot. Two clients can do this for the same trainer and the same slot within milliseconds of each other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your app does this in two steps:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SELECT to check the slot is free&lt;br&gt;
INSERT the booking&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;then both requests can pass step 1 before either one reaches step 2. Result: a double booking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Checking in the frontend or in your API code doesn't fix it, because the race happens between your two queries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why not just a unique constraint?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A unique constraint works if every booking uses exactly the same start time. It breaks down quickly:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Services have different durations (30 min, 60 min), so bookings overlap without being equal.&lt;br&gt;
Group classes allow several people in the same slot, up to a capacity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An exclusion constraint can handle simple overlaps, but group capacity ("up to 10 people") doesn't fit that model nicely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The approach: lock, then check, inside the database&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I put the check in a BEFORE INSERT trigger on the bookings table, and I take a transaction-level advisory lock first. The lock key is the staff member plus the date:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sql&lt;br&gt;
-- Simplified. The real version also handles group capacity and expired holds.&lt;br&gt;
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION check_booking_availability()&lt;br&gt;
RETURNS trigger&lt;br&gt;
LANGUAGE plpgsql&lt;br&gt;
AS $$&lt;br&gt;
DECLARE&lt;br&gt;
overlapping integer;&lt;br&gt;
BEGIN&lt;br&gt;
-- Serialize concurrent bookings for the same staff member on the same day.&lt;br&gt;
PERFORM pg_advisory_xact_lock(&lt;br&gt;
hashtextextended(NEW.staff_id::text || NEW.booking_date::text, 0)&lt;br&gt;
);&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SELECT count(*) INTO overlapping&lt;br&gt;
FROM bookings b&lt;br&gt;
WHERE b.staff_id = NEW.staff_id&lt;br&gt;
AND b.booking_date = NEW.booking_date&lt;br&gt;
AND b.status IN ('pending', 'confirmed')&lt;br&gt;
AND b.start_time &amp;lt; NEW.end_time&lt;br&gt;
AND b.end_time &amp;gt; NEW.start_time;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;IF overlapping &amp;gt; 0 THEN&lt;br&gt;
RAISE EXCEPTION 'This time slot is no longer available';&lt;br&gt;
END IF;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;RETURN NEW;&lt;br&gt;
END;&lt;br&gt;
$$;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CREATE TRIGGER bookings_check_availability&lt;br&gt;
BEFORE INSERT ON bookings&lt;br&gt;
FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION check_booking_availability();&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What this gives you:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The advisory lock is held until the transaction ends. A second booking for the same staff member and day waits for the first to commit or roll back, then runs its own check and sees the first booking.&lt;br&gt;
Different staff members, or different days, use different lock keys, so they don't block each other.&lt;br&gt;
The rule lives in the database, so it applies no matter which client inserts (your API, an admin script, a future mobile app).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the app, when the trigger raises the exception, the booking request fails and the client sees a message asking them to pick another slot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Group classes and capacity&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For group classes, the check changes from "any overlap blocks" to "count the people already in this class and compare with capacity". Same lock, same trigger, different condition.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Temporary holds for paid bookings&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If a service requires payment, I create the booking as pending with a hold_expires_at timestamp while the client pays. The availability check ignores pending bookings whose hold has expired, so an abandoned checkout doesn't block a slot forever:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sql&lt;br&gt;
AND NOT (b.status = 'pending'&lt;br&gt;
AND b.hold_expires_at IS NOT NULL&lt;br&gt;
AND b.hold_expires_at &amp;lt; now())&lt;br&gt;
Things I'd warn you about&lt;br&gt;
Test the race, don't assume it. Fire two inserts for the same slot in parallel (two terminals, or a small script) and confirm only one succeeds.&lt;br&gt;
Advisory locks are application-defined. Nothing stops other code from inserting without going through the trigger path, so keep the check in the trigger and not in the app only.&lt;br&gt;
Time zones. Store timestamps in UTC and convert per business. It's easy to get the "day" wrong near midnight.&lt;br&gt;
Row Level Security still matters. The trigger prevents double bookings; RLS policies decide who can create or cancel a booking at all.&lt;br&gt;
Wrapping up&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The core idea is small: lock the resource, then check, then insert, all in one transaction. Everything else (capacity, holds, payments) builds on that.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I packaged this booking engine, the owner dashboard and the public booking page as a source-code starter kit for developers who build booking apps for clients. It's $99 one-time. The known limits are listed upfront: the CMI (Moroccan gateway) integration is a mock, Stripe is test mode only, and there's no automated test suite.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;30-second demo: &lt;a href="https://youtube.com/shorts/SKSHpPnNcOQ" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://youtube.com/shorts/SKSHpPnNcOQ&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Full walkthrough: &lt;a href="https://youtu.be/83ZVDX_zGSg" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://youtu.be/83ZVDX_zGSg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Details and live demo: &lt;a href="https://grow-roots-landing.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://grow-roots-landing.vercel.app&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you've solved double bookings differently (exclusion constraints, SELECT ... FOR UPDATE, queues), I'd like to hear what worked for you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I posted about the eight small sites I build on the side, and someone in the comments said culdesac.site was their favourite. Their take: the name already sounds like a quiet dead-end street where weird little corners of the web live. That's pretty much the whole idea, so here's how it works.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What it is
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You land on a teal 1997 desktop with one grey window and one button: &lt;strong&gt;find me somewhere&lt;/strong&gt;. Press it and a little browser window opens on a small site somebody made. Hit Next for another one. Visit opens the real thing in a new tab. On a phone you just swipe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's not a new idea. The Useless Web and a pile of random-site buttons have done this for over a decade. The mechanic was never going to be the interesting part. The list is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The list
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are 975 sites in it right now, and every description was written fresh for this. None are copied from wherever the link came from. Each one gets a label: oddity, toy, ambient, time-capsule, vista, rabbit-hole, garden or tool. They're labels, not filters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"Garden" is for personal sites and digital gardens, and those get a stricter bar since they belong to real people. The site has to be alive, and the blurb has to say what the notes are actually about.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few from the oddity pile: Eel Slap, Endless Horse, Pointer Pointer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The whole catalog is one JSON file. No CMS, no database for the list. To add a site I append an object, write a blurb and run the link checker.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How the button picks
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The draw is uniform over the sites your device hasn't been sent to in the last 24 hours. That "seen" list lives in localStorage as a list of URLs and one timestamp, and that's it. No scoring, nothing that reads what you saved or clicked.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One honest exception: through the end of the year, eight slots in your first 45 presses are held for my own sites (dialup.rip, salvage.run and the rest). Every other press is uniform, and the hold ends by date on its own, so it can't quietly turn permanent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Under the hood
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React and Vite on Vercel, plus a few small serverless functions for counters, reports and suggestions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No cookies, no accounts. Saved sites stay on your device and never get sent anywhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The previews in the window are snapshots I capture with a real browser, shrunk to small WebP files and served from culdesac.site, so looking at one tells the destination nothing. If a site won't photograph cleanly, you get the title and blurb instead of a broken image.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Every site also has its own prerendered page at &lt;code&gt;/site/&amp;lt;slug&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. The app routes on the hash, so without those, a search engine would basically see one page. I also dropped the SPA catch-all rewrite, so a mistyped URL gets a real 404 instead of the homepage with a 200.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Go stumble
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you miss StumbleUpon, or just want five minutes somewhere that isn't a feed, press the button: &lt;a href="https://culdesac.site" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://culdesac.site&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Got a weird little site, or know one? There's a "Suggest a site" icon on the desktop. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our app, HypeFox, renders short videos from code: a model writes a scene file in JSON, and Remotion turns it into 1080×1920 frames on cloud containers. Last week we shipped an editor where people change a video and see the result right away. These are our notes from running the same video code in two places.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The setup
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The cloud renders with Remotion 4.0.536 on containers that sleep when there's no work (we wrote about that part &lt;a href="https://dev.to/mattiamaggioni/rendering-ai-short-videos-on-containers-that-switch-off-after-2-minutes-our-setup-and-real-costs-4cek"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The editor plays the video with Remotion's Player: same version, same style components. No style exists twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Whatever the person changes is stored as overrides on top of the scene file: captions, texts, colors, transitions, elements. A save sends the overrides, and the cloud renders with the same code and the same overrides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Prove they match before building any UI
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first thing we built was not a button. It was a check: two real videos, one with a generated voice and one cut from a person's footage, played by the Player in the browser and rendered by the same renderer we run in the cloud, then compared frame by frame. They matched.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every later feature had to pass the same kind of test. Transitions, for example: with no transition set, the new code must produce frames identical to the old code. We compare 27 frames per example, at the scene boundaries and a few frames around them, pixel by pixel, in every style.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Ship only the style you open
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Six styles in one bundle came to almost 1 MB compressed. Split per style, the editor downloads 209 to 602 KB compressed, depending on the style of the video you open.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Phones are the real test
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Measured on an iPhone: three styles preview at 30 fps, one at 28, one at 21 and the heaviest at 18. We kept the live preview for all of them. A few dropped frames in a preview are fine. A preview that doesn't match the final video is not.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Things that bit us
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Music that restarted every tenth of a second.&lt;/strong&gt; Static assets on Cloudflare answered every request with a 200 and the whole file, never a 206 for a &lt;code&gt;Range&lt;/code&gt; request. Chrome then treated the audio as not seekable, and a track that starts in the middle kept seeking forever. A Worker now serves audio and video with real &lt;code&gt;Range&lt;/code&gt; support (206, &lt;code&gt;Content-Range&lt;/code&gt;, 416 when out of range). The seekable range went from &lt;code&gt;[0,0]&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;[0,180]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fonts from a third party.&lt;/strong&gt; The styles loaded fonts from Google Fonts. Our content security policy would have blocked them, and we'd rather not tell Google who opens the editor. The Worker fetches each font once, caches it and serves it from our own domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A glyph the cloud didn't have.&lt;/strong&gt; A typewriter caption style used "▍" as the cursor. It looked fine on a Mac. The cloud's fonts don't have it, so it rendered as an empty box. It's "_" now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Transitions must not move the captions.&lt;/strong&gt; When someone sets a transition between two scenes, the style cuts straight at that boundary and the effect is applied to the picture only. Captions and overlays stay still.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Overlays that follow words
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;People don't think "at 7.4 seconds". They think "when I say rent". So a text, sticker or shape can be anchored to a spoken word, using the word timings from the voice step. When a sentence changes or a cut moves, the overlay moves with its word.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What a save costs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only the sentences that changed go back to the voice. The render runs on the same containers as new videos. A save costs about a cent of container time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How do you preview server-rendered media: the same code in the browser, or a fast low-res render?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Written with the help of an AI assistant, from our own code, notes and measurements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Production Application:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://api-casetracker.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://api-casetracker.vercel.app&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Source Code:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/mohinth-project/api-casetracker" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;FastAPI Backend &amp;amp; React TypeScript Atelier Architecture&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Memory Infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://docs.hindsight.vectorize.io" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hindsight Client by Vectorize&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


1. The 4-Hour "Déjà Vu" in Enterprise API Support
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you have ever worked in technical support for an enterprise API platform, this scenario will feel painfully familiar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is 2:15 AM. A priority-one incident is filed by an enterprise client:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;HTTP 401 Unauthorized: Invalid Token during Scheduled Batch Sync&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A support engineer logs in, dives into the reverse proxy logs, checks OAuth2 client credentials, inspects the token lifetime, and checks the Redis cache. Four hours and twenty minutes later, they pinpoint the root cause:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;The client's batch sync script had a token cache expiry buffer that expired five minutes before the gateway revoked the JWT.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The engineer gives the client the fix: set &lt;code&gt;token_ttl_buffer_seconds = 300&lt;/code&gt;. The ticket is closed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Three weeks later, the exact same client spins up a new microservice in staging and makes the exact same configuration mistake. But this time, a different engineer is on call. They have no idea this was already diagnosed. &lt;strong&gt;They spend another four hours rediscovering the exact same solution.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


The Core Problem: Architectural Divergence
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In modern B2B SaaS, no two enterprise customers run the same architecture:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Customer A&lt;/strong&gt; runs an older REST API &lt;code&gt;v2.1&lt;/code&gt; with OAuth2 Bearer tokens on AWS EU.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Customer B&lt;/strong&gt; runs an enterprise API &lt;code&gt;v1.9&lt;/code&gt; over Mutual TLS (&lt;code&gt;mTLS&lt;/code&gt;) with strict corporate truststores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Customer C&lt;/strong&gt; runs a preview API &lt;code&gt;v3.0-rc&lt;/code&gt; with HIPAA payload encryption envelopes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When an error message like &lt;code&gt;401 Unauthorized&lt;/code&gt; appears, generic LLMs or shared knowledge bases fail catastrophically because they treat all customers identically. Recommending Customer A's OAuth token fix to Customer B's mTLS certificate issue breaks production.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We built &lt;strong&gt;API CaseTracker&lt;/strong&gt; to solve this once and for all.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


2. The Concrete Before vs. After
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Metric / Scenario&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Before API CaseTracker&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;After API CaseTracker (with Hindsight)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Impact&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mean Time to Resolution (MTTR)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;4.2 hours&lt;/strong&gt; per recurrent incident&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;120 milliseconds&lt;/strong&gt; recall + 2 min review&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;99.2% time reduction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Tenant Contamination&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;High risk (shared wiki or single vector index)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;0% risk&lt;/strong&gt; (Isolated &lt;code&gt;casetracker-{customer_id}&lt;/code&gt; banks)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strict architectural privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Handling Novel Issues&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Hallucinated LLM suggestions&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero-Hallucination Protocol&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;needs_investigation: true&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safe, non-speculative engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Institutional Knowledge Retention&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lost in closed tickets and Slack threads&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Learning Loop&lt;/strong&gt; (One-click memory retention)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge compounds permanently&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


3. How Hindsight Powers Customer-Isolated Memory
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pools all documents into a single global vector index. In multi-tenant enterprise software, this is dangerous: querying a symptom can inadvertently recall another customer's private API keys, endpoints, or network topology.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.hindsight.vectorize.io" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hindsight&lt;/a&gt; solves this at the architectural layer through &lt;strong&gt;dedicated Memory Banks&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;                       ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           API CaseTracker Gateway                 │
└─────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┘
│
┌───────────────┴───────────────┐
│ Extract Scope: customer_id    │
└───────────────┬───────────────┘
▼
Targeted Memory Bank: casetracker-{customer_id}
┌────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┐
▼                                ▼                                ▼
Bank: casetracker-cust_apex      Bank: casetracker-cust_beacon    Bank: casetracker-cust_catalyst
[Apex Retail Group Scope]        [Beacon Financial Scope]         [Catalyst Health Scope]
• OAuth2 PKCE TTL Drift          • mTLS CA Truststore Expiry      • JWE Payload GCM Ciphers
• JWKS Poll Intervals            • Intermediate DigiCert Bundles  • HIPAA Envelope Timings
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every customer has an isolated bank: &lt;code&gt;casetracker-{customer_id}&lt;/code&gt;. When an incident is analyzed, Hindsight queries &lt;strong&gt;only&lt;/strong&gt; that customer's partitioned memory bank.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


4. Code Implementation: The 4 Core Building Blocks
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Snippet 1: Initializing the Hindsight Client &amp;amp; Scoped Memory Banks
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;code&gt;backend/app/hindsight_service.py&lt;/code&gt;, we initialize the official &lt;code&gt;hindsight-client&lt;/code&gt; Python SDK and scope every operation to the customer's partition:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;logging&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;HindsightClient&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;app.config&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;settings&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;logging&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getLogger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;casetracker.hindsight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;HindsightService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;__init__&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;api_key&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;HINDSIGHT_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;base_url&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;HINDSIGHT_BASE_URL&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;api_key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Initialize official Hindsight Cloud SDK
&lt;/span&gt;            &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;HindsightClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;api_key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;api_key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;span class="n"&gt;base_url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;base_url&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_live&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;info&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Connected to live Hindsight Cloud Memory Engine.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;is_live&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;warning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;No HINDSIGHT_API_KEY set; running in local demo memory mode.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;get_bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Enforce strict memory isolation per customer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;clean_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;strip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;lower&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;casetracker-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;clean_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h3&gt;


Snippet 2: Memory Recall with the Zero-Hallucination Guardrail
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;code&gt;backend/app/routes/analyze.py&lt;/code&gt;, we query Hindsight. If the memory confidence does not meet our minimum threshold ($\ge 0.70$), the system explicitly refuses to guess:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fastapi&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;APIRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;HTTPException&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;app.models&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;AnalyzeRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;AnalyzeResponse&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;app.hindsight_service&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_service&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;router&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;APIRouter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;prefix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;/api/issues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tags&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Diagnostics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@router.post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;/analyze&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response_model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;AnalyzeResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;analyze_issue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;AnalyzeRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get_bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;query_text&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;error_message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;endpoint&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; (symptoms: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;symptoms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 1. Recall historical incidents strictly within customer's memory bank
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="n"&gt;recall_result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;recall&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;span class="n"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;query_text&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 2. Strict Zero-Hallucination Protocol
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;recall_result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;recall_result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;confidence&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.70&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AnalyzeResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;needs_investigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;confidence_score&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;recall_result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;confidence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;matching_case_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;recall_result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;case_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;diagnosis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;recall_result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;root_cause&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;suggested_fix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;recall_result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;verified_fix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;architectural_context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Verified fix for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; on API &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;api_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 3. Novel issue fallback - Never hallucinate a remedy
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AnalyzeResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;needs_investigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;confidence_score&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.25&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;diagnosis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;No verified resolution found in bank &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;recommendation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Escalate to Tier-3 support engineer for manual forensic investigation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h3&gt;


Snippet 3: The Continuous Learning Loop (Memory Retention)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a human engineer identifies the true root cause and verified fix, they submit it to &lt;code&gt;POST /api/issues/{id}/resolution&lt;/code&gt;. The system permanently commits the fix into Hindsight via &lt;code&gt;retain()&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@router.post&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;/{issue_id}/resolution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;retain_resolution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;issue_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ResolutionSubmission&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get_bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;memory_document&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;case_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;issue_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;symptoms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;symptoms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;root_cause&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;root_cause&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;verified_fix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;verified_fix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;verified_by&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;verified_by&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;api_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;api_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;api_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;api_version&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environment&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Commit truth into Hindsight persistent memory
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="n"&gt;retain_response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;retain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;memory_document&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;info&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Retained &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;issue_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt; in bank &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;. Hindsight ID: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;retain_response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;retained&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;case_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;issue_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h3&gt;


Snippet 4: Pydantic Data Contract
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;code&gt;backend/app/models.py&lt;/code&gt;, strict validation guarantees data integrity across the pipeline:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pydantic&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseModel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Field&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;typing&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;AnalyzeResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;BaseModel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;needs_investigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;bool&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Flag indicating whether manual human investigation is required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;confidence_score&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;float&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;le&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Hindsight similarity confidence score&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;matching_case_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;diagnosis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;suggested_fix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;architectural_context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


5. Walkthrough of the Three Core Flows
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Known Issue with Prior Fix (Apex Retail Group)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Symptom:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;401 Unauthorized&lt;/code&gt; during batch invoice sync on &lt;code&gt;v2.4&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Action:&lt;/strong&gt; Engineer selects Apex Retail and clicks &lt;strong&gt;Run Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Result:&lt;/strong&gt; In 120ms, Hindsight recalls &lt;code&gt;CASE-1082&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Verified Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Flush Redis OAuth token cache on the webhook proxy and set &lt;code&gt;jwks_poll_interval_seconds&lt;/code&gt; to 300. &lt;code&gt;needs_investigation: false&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Customer Memory Isolation (Beacon Financial Systems)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Symptom:&lt;/strong&gt; The exact same error: &lt;code&gt;401 Unauthorized&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Action:&lt;/strong&gt; Engineer selects Beacon Financial and clicks &lt;strong&gt;Run Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Result:&lt;/strong&gt; Because Beacon uses mTLS on &lt;code&gt;v1.9&lt;/code&gt;, querying Beacon's isolated memory bank ignores Apex completely and recalls &lt;code&gt;CASE-1094&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Verified Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Append DigiCert Global Root G2 to &lt;code&gt;/etc/ssl/certs/corporate-truststore.pem&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Proof:&lt;/strong&gt; Same symptom → customer-specific diagnosis → zero cross-tenant contamination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Novel Issue &amp;amp; The Learning Loop (Catalyst Health Cloud)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Symptom:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;504 Gateway Timeout during batch transaction export&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;v3.0-rc&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Action:&lt;/strong&gt; Analyzed against Catalyst's memory bank.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Result:&lt;/strong&gt; No verified record exists. Returns &lt;code&gt;needs_investigation: true&lt;/code&gt; with 25% confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Learning Loop:&lt;/strong&gt; The engineer diagnoses a database read-replica query lag, creates a compound index &lt;code&gt;(organization_id, export_status, created_at)&lt;/code&gt;, and clicks &lt;strong&gt;Confirm &amp;amp; Retain Fix&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Verification:&lt;/strong&gt; Re-running the exact same query immediately returns the new compound index fix with 95% confidence!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


6. Four Engineering Lessons We Learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Memory Scoping Must Precede Vector Embedding:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Filtering vector search by metadata after embedding search is prone to leakage or performance degradation. Defining discrete memory banks per customer at the storage level (&lt;code&gt;casetracker-{customer_id}&lt;/code&gt;) guarantees physical isolation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Refusing to Answer is Better Than Hallucinating:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
In mission-critical infrastructure, a wrong AI suggestion can cause cascading downtime. Setting a confidence floor of &lt;code&gt;0.70&lt;/code&gt; and defaulting to &lt;code&gt;needs_investigation: true&lt;/code&gt; built trust with engineers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the Human in the Learning Loop:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Autonomous AI should not automatically commit fixes to memory. A human engineer must verify that a fix worked in production before retaining it into Hindsight.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Static Bundling in Python Serverless Needs Explicit MIME Mapping:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
When deploying a combined FastAPI + React Vite application on serverless platforms like Vercel, static rewrite rules must be explicitly handled by ASGI middleware with &lt;code&gt;keep_blank_values=True&lt;/code&gt; to prevent JavaScript chunks from being served as &lt;code&gt;text/html&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


7. Visual Artifacts &amp;amp; Proof from the Live System
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Overview Architecture &amp;amp; Verified Metrics
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqed2k8s3zzq65vt9byt8.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqed2k8s3zzq65vt9byt8.jpg" alt="API CaseTracker Architecture Overview" width="800" height="943"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Figure 1: The Atelier architecture overview showing the 3-step Hindsight customer memory pipeline and verified metrics (88.6% recall rate, 4.2 hours saved per incident, 100% isolation, 0% hallucinations).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Flow 1A: Instant Memory Recall for Apex Retail
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwx6q5xiehmgye40yq8wa.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fwx6q5xiehmgye40yq8wa.jpg" alt="Flow 1A: Instant Recall for Apex Retail" width="800" height="697"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Figure 2: Instant recall of CASE-1082 for Apex Retail with 99% match score, delivering the verified Redis token cache flush proposal.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Flow 1B: Customer Scope Isolation for Beacon Financial
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F926atcn75dv22rv54nze.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F926atcn75dv22rv54nze.jpg" alt="Flow 1B: Customer Isolation for Beacon Financial" width="800" height="678"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Figure 3: Beacon Financial receiving a customer-specific mTLS certificate fix for the exact same 401 symptom without memory bleed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Flow 2 &amp;amp; 3: Zero-Hallucination &amp;amp; The Continuous Learning Loop
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqi29mdibiv1d56mwv7pi.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqi29mdibiv1d56mwv7pi.jpg" alt="Flow 2 and 3: Zero-Hallucination and Learning Loop" width="800" height="679"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Figure 4: Zero-hallucination escalation for novel issues, ready for the engineer to sign off and permanently commit the fix into Hindsight.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


8. References &amp;amp; Documentation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.hindsight.vectorize.io" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hindsight Client Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;FastAPI Framework Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://vite.dev/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Vite Next Generation Frontend Tooling&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://api-casetracker.vercel.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Live Production Deployment&lt;/a&gt;
itha posu pothum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I get this question a lot, so I’ll answer it from what I actually did.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On the recruitment ATS/CRM I worked on, the frontend was first built in WeWeb. Later we rebuilt the whole frontend in React 19 + TypeScript, and most of that work was done with Claude Code. So I’ve used both on the same product, with real users.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My answer is simple: if you’ve never coded before, start with WeWeb. If you already have some notions of code, start with React.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why WeWeb if you’ve never coded
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;WeWeb is easy to pick up. You put elements on a page, connect them to your data, and add workflows that run when someone clicks a button or submits a form.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What I like is that it teaches you how a frontend works while you build:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you pick up in WeWeb:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;how a page fetches data from an API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;where that data is kept while the page is open&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;workflows: when this happens, do this, then that&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;variables and conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;what to do when a request fails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You do the same things in React later. In WeWeb you just do them visually first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It’s also a good option if you don’t want to vibe-code everything with AI. You build each part yourself, so you understand what you made. (I wrote more about that in &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/blog/low-code-vs-vibe-coding/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;low-code or vibe coding&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why React is easier to get into now
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few years ago React was harder to start with. You had to set up the project, learn the tooling and write everything by hand before anything worked.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With Claude Code that’s different. You describe the page, it writes the components, and you review and fix what it wrote. You can build a lot more in a lot less time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That’s how we did our migration. We added React pages one by one while the WeWeb app was still running, until React was the whole frontend. We used TanStack Query, React Hook Form, Zod and React Router.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WeWeb app in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React pages added one by one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both running during the migration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React becomes the whole frontend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;How we moved from WeWeb to React&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a big app that keeps growing, I’d pick React today because you have full control over the code. (More on my &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/react-developer/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React work&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


React is harder to debug
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In WeWeb, when something breaks, you open the workflow and check each step. You can see what the API returned and which variable is empty.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In React the problem can be in a component, a hook, the state, the cache, a request or a type. You check the console and the network tab, and follow the data through several files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If AI wrote a big part of the code, a beginner will have a hard time here, because you’re debugging code you didn’t write and don’t fully understand yet. That’s where I see most people get stuck.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WeWeb&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you see each workflow step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you see what the API returned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fewer places for a bug to hide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;less freedom when the app gets big&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;full control over the code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI writes it much faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;bugs can be spread across files&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you need to read code to fix it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Which one to start with
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start with WeWeb if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you’ve never written code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you want to see how data and workflows work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you want to build something real soon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you don’t want AI doing everything for you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start with React if&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you already know some code, even a little&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you studied programming or tried it before&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you want to learn the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;you plan to build bigger apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Starting with WeWeb doesn’t lock you in. When you move to React later, you’ll already know how data is fetched, what state is and how a workflow runs, so it’s mostly about learning to write it as code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you already know some code, I wouldn’t spend months in a visual tool. Go to React, use AI to go faster, and read what it writes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a large frontend I’d use React today. But WeWeb got us far quickly, and I’d still recommend it to someone who has never coded. (For the bigger picture, see &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/blog/low-code-vs-full-code/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;low-code vs full-code&lt;/a&gt;.)&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;I first posted this &lt;a href="https://bilelabdelmoula.dev/blog/weweb-vs-react/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;on my blog&lt;/a&gt;, where it’s also in French and Arabic. What did you start with, and would you pick the same again?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the member list in almost any app. Most people never upload a photo, so you see a column of identical grey silhouettes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8h75fdqsh8y9mo4sgtfq.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F8h75fdqsh8y9mo4sgtfq.png" alt="when not to use it" width="800" height="377"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The usual fixes each come with a catch:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Initials&lt;/strong&gt; work until two people are both "JS". And white letters on bright tiles often fail contrast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Random colors&lt;/strong&gt; change on every render, unless you add a database column to store them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Generated avatars&lt;/strong&gt; are the right idea, but many use &lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt; or hard-coded SVG IDs. Then the server draws one face, the browser draws another, and your console fills with hydration warnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I wanted avatars I would never have to think about again. Same input, same bytes, on every server, in every browser and in every release. That became &lt;a href="https://github.com/Inlaylab/Opaline" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Opaline&lt;/a&gt;. This post covers what it gives you, how to use it, and the engineering that makes the promise hold.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why you might want it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;You want&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What Opaline does&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Users you can tell apart&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Each seed gets its own face, colors and shape. Five styles.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Avatars that never change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Same seed and options give a byte-identical SVG for all of 1.x, checked in CI&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No hydration warnings&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Server and client produce the same markup. Tested in Next, Nuxt, SvelteKit and Angular SSR.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One library across your stack&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One core and components for React 18+, Vue 3.5+, Svelte 5.20+, Angular 20–22, plus a Web Component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A small bundle&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Core is &lt;strong&gt;1.27 kB&lt;/strong&gt; gzipped with zero dependencies. With the largest style it's 5.57 kB.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Photos when users have them&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Pass &lt;code&gt;src&lt;/code&gt;. If it's missing or broken, the generated face stays.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Brand colors and dark mode&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Colors are CSS variables, so you restyle without regenerating&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Accessible initials&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Letters clear WCAG AA (4.5:1) on every palette, checked for 2,100 seed/palette pairs&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No license review&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;MIT for the code &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; the art&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Using it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install the package for your framework. Each one pulls in the core.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm i @inlaylab/opaline-react   &lt;span class="c"&gt;# or -vue, -svelte, -angular, -element&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt; (server-component safe, React 18 or later):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AvatarGroup&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline-react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline/clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;look&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;photo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AvatarGroup&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;look&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;members&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;alt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Project members&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vue 3.5+ / Nuxt:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight vue"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:seed=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"user.email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:look=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"clay"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"user.photo"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;:alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"user.name"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Svelte 5.20+ / SvelteKit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight svelte"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;seed=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;look=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;src=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;photo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Angular 20–22&lt;/strong&gt; (standalone, OnPush, works zoneless):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;op-avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;[seed]=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;[look]=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"clay"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;[src]=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"photo"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No framework:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;script &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;type=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"module"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline-element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;opaline-avatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;seed=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"ada@inlay.dev"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;look=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"clay"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;finish=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"gloss"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;size=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"64"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;alt=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/opaline-avatar&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No DOM at all.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;createAvatar&lt;/code&gt; returns a plain string, so it works in an API route, a build script or an email template:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline/clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;ada@inlay.dev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;hood&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ears&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;bunny&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flk8bcu9lnrdlwy57g8lq.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Flk8bcu9lnrdlwy57g8lq.png" alt="createAvatar code next to the avatar it generates" width="800" height="400"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any option you set pins that part of the avatar. The seed fills in the rest.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Need a PNG for an OG card, a push notification or a profile-photo upload? &lt;code&gt;toPng&lt;/code&gt; (688 B) does it in the browser with no dependencies:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toPng&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@inlaylab/opaline/png&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;blob&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;toPng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;512&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now the interesting part: how "same bytes everywhere" actually holds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. The seed is the only input, so normalize it first
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users type &lt;code&gt;Ada@Inlay.dev&lt;/code&gt; with a trailing space on one form and &lt;code&gt;ada@inlay.dev&lt;/code&gt; on another. If those give different faces, you get a bug report. So every seed goes through this first:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;EMAIL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/^&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;[^\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;[^\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;@&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;+$/&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;normalizeSeed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;''&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;normalize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;NFC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;EMAIL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLowerCase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;NFC matters more than it looks. &lt;code&gt;Zoë&lt;/code&gt; can arrive as one code point (&lt;code&gt;ë&lt;/code&gt;) or two (&lt;code&gt;e&lt;/code&gt; plus a combining diaeresis), depending on the OS and keyboard. Without NFC those are two different people.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only emails are lower-cased. Usernames like &lt;code&gt;Ada&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;ada&lt;/code&gt; can be different accounts, so they keep their case.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. No Math.random(): a seeded PRNG with forks
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The seed goes through &lt;strong&gt;xmur3&lt;/strong&gt;, a small string hash, which seeds &lt;strong&gt;sfc32&lt;/strong&gt;, a fast 32-bit PRNG. Both fit in a few lines and give identical results on every JavaScript engine, because they use only &lt;code&gt;Math.imul&lt;/code&gt;, shifts and &lt;code&gt;| 0&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createRng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Rng&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;xmur3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;sfc32&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Early sfc32 outputs are weakly mixed; skip them.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;++&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;float&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// A fork depends only on the seed and label, never on earlier draws.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;fork&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createRng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;u0000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;fork&lt;/code&gt; line is the most important decision in the library.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A naive generator draws everything from one stream: shape, then color, then eyes, then mouth. Now add a new eyebrow option in a later release. It takes one draw from the stream, and every draw after it shifts. &lt;strong&gt;Every existing user's mouth changes.&lt;/strong&gt; That's a breaking change you didn't mean to ship.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With forks, each feature gets its own stream, keyed by the seed and a label:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rng&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fork&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;color&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;pick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;palette&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;hues&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;float&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;fork('color')&lt;/code&gt; gives the same numbers whether it's called first or last, or after ten new features. New features get new labels. Old faces never move.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;\u0000&lt;/code&gt; separator stops a seed of &lt;code&gt;"ab"&lt;/code&gt; with label &lt;code&gt;"c"&lt;/code&gt; from colliding with seed &lt;code&gt;"a"&lt;/code&gt; and label &lt;code&gt;"bc"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. SVG IDs that are unique per page and identical across hydration
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SVG gradients and filters need &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;s. That creates two separate bugs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Two avatars on one page share &lt;code&gt;id="grad"&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; The second one silently uses the first one's gradient, so the wrong colors appear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The server and the client invent different IDs.&lt;/strong&gt; You get a hydration mismatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Opaline builds every ID from two parts:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createIds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;u0000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;u0000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;stableStringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;instance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// id('grad') -&amp;gt; "a&amp;lt;7-char hash&amp;gt;-grad-&amp;lt;instance&amp;gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The prefix&lt;/strong&gt; is a hash of the seed, the style and the options. The same seed with different options never shares &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;defs&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;stableStringify&lt;/code&gt; sorts the keys, so option order never matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The instance suffix&lt;/strong&gt; comes from each framework's SSR-safe ID primitive:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Package&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Instance from&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Minimum version&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;useId()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React 18, the version that introduced &lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vue&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;useId()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Vue 3.5. Multiple apps on a page set &lt;code&gt;app.config.idPrefix&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Svelte&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;$props.id()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Svelte 5.20&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Angular&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;An injectable per-app counter. Server and client render in the same order, so the numbers match.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Angular 20&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Web Component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A module counter. There is no SSR, so only uniqueness matters.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Any modern browser&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That table is also why the minimum versions are what they are. &lt;strong&gt;1.1.2&lt;/strong&gt; lowered React to 18 for exactly this reason: &lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt; exists there, so nothing else was blocking it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Defaults are invisible
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One rule turned out to matter a lot: &lt;strong&gt;an option set to its default must give byte-for-byte the same output as leaving it unset.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without that rule, &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar finish="soft"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Avatar&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; hash to different ID prefixes, so a refactor that spells out a default changes your markup. Each style declares its defaults, and &lt;code&gt;createAvatar&lt;/code&gt; drops matching values before hashing:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;defaults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;k&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;stableStringify&lt;/code&gt; also skips &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; values. Wrappers pass every prop through, and &lt;code&gt;{ shape: undefined }&lt;/code&gt; must not hash differently from &lt;code&gt;{}&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Proof, not promises
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"Deterministic" is an easy word to write in a README. Here is how the repo checks it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


A frozen checksum file: 4,000 hashes
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0e14zxgfssidzpuqfg8y.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F0e14zxgfssidzpuqfg8y.png" alt="SSR" width="800" height="326"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;frozen-1.json&lt;/code&gt; holds 4,000 SHA-256 digests (first 16 hex characters):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;100 seeds&lt;/strong&gt; shaped like real input: emails, &lt;code&gt;Person B12&lt;/code&gt;-style names, base36 IDs, plain numbers, and Unicode with emoji (&lt;code&gt;Zoë Nguyễn 4 😀&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;40 option sets&lt;/strong&gt; across all five styles: every finish, every shape, palettes, hood and ears, custom initials text.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`1.x output is frozen: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;FROZEN_SEEDS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createAvatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;opts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;changed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;FROZEN_SEEDS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;manifest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]?.[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;changed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Output changed for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;...`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toEqual&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If one byte of one avatar changes, CI fails and names the seed. A second test checks that the manifest still covers every case, so nobody can make the guarantee pass by deleting rows. The only way to change the output is to regenerate the file on purpose, and that means a major version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That's what lets you cache an avatar on a CDN forever, store the SVG in a database, or put it in an email that will be opened in three years.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Real SSR apps, hydrated in a real browser
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Four sample apps live in the repo: &lt;strong&gt;Next (App Router, RSC), Nuxt, SvelteKit and Angular SSR (zoneless)&lt;/strong&gt;. For each one, Playwright:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;starts the production server and fetches the HTML;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;asserts that every &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; in the page is unique, and that the named avatar has &lt;code&gt;role="img"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;aria-label&lt;/code&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;loads the page in Chromium and fails on any console message matching &lt;code&gt;/hydrat/i&lt;/code&gt;, any error and any page exception;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;compares the hydrated DOM with the server HTML&lt;/strong&gt;: every avatar's root attributes and its &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;svg&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; must be exactly what the server sent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step 4 exists because of something I found while writing step 3. &lt;strong&gt;Production Svelte repairs a hydration mismatch silently.&lt;/strong&gt; No warning, no error. The page looks fine, the console is clean, and the bug is invisible. Watching the console isn't enough. You have to diff the DOM.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Size, enforced
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;size-limit&lt;/code&gt; runs in CI with a budget for every entry point. These are today's numbers, minified and gzipped:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Import&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Size&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Budget&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;createAvatar&lt;/code&gt; (core)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1.27 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Aura&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2.52 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Initials&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2.86 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Morph&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4.90 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Gradient&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5.13 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5.25 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;core + Clay&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5.57 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;8 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React wrapper (avatar + group)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;854 B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1.5 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;PNG export&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;688 B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1 kB&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Styles are separate imports, so you only ship the ones you use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Speed
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A perf test builds 500 Clay avatars with the gloss finish, the heaviest combination. It warms the JIT, then keeps the best of five runs. On my laptop (Node 24) that's &lt;strong&gt;56–63 ms, about 120 µs per avatar&lt;/strong&gt;. CI fails above 250 ms, so a slow shared runner doesn't flake the build. A member list of 200 people costs you around 25 ms of CPU, once.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What broke along the way
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I broke my own promise once, on purpose.&lt;/strong&gt; 1.1.0 shipped Initials with white letters. On the brightest tiles that was as low as &lt;strong&gt;1.9:1&lt;/strong&gt; contrast, far below the 4.5:1 that WCAG AA asks for. Shipping unreadable letters for the rest of 1.x seemed worse than changing them. So 1.1.1 changed exactly one thing: the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;text&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; fill on non-pastel palettes is now a deep shade of the tile's own hue. Nothing else changed: no shapes, no other styles. A new test checks 300 seeds on each of the 7 palettes and fails if any pair falls below 4.5:1. The README lists this as the one deliberate exception.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt; output isn't a valid SVG ID fragment.&lt;/strong&gt; Depending on the version, React's IDs contain characters such as &lt;code&gt;:&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;:r1:&lt;/code&gt; in React 18) or &lt;code&gt;«»&lt;/code&gt;. Those characters cause trouble inside &lt;code&gt;url(#…)&lt;/code&gt; references, so the wrapper strips everything except word characters and dashes before it uses the suffix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; changed the hash.&lt;/strong&gt; Wrappers forward every prop, so the core saw &lt;code&gt;{ shape: undefined }&lt;/code&gt; and hashed it differently from &lt;code&gt;{}&lt;/code&gt;. The result was a different ID prefix for the same avatar, depending on which wrapper rendered it. That's why &lt;code&gt;stableStringify&lt;/code&gt; now filters &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A silent Svelte fix hid a real mismatch&lt;/strong&gt;, as described above. That's why the e2e diffs the DOM and doesn't trust the console.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When not to use it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want dozens of art styles, or an image URL from a hosted HTTP API with no code at all: use &lt;a href="https://www.dicebear.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;DiceBear&lt;/a&gt;. It's excellent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You're React-only and want minimal abstract shapes in your exact brand palette: &lt;a href="https://boringavatars.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Boring Avatars&lt;/a&gt; is lovely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need server-side PNG with zero setup: Opaline's &lt;code&gt;forRaster()&lt;/code&gt; prepares the SVG, but you still bring a rasterizer such as &lt;code&gt;@resvg/resvg-js&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://inlaylab.github.io/Opaline/compare/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;comparison page&lt;/a&gt; goes row by row, including the rows where the others win.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Try it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🎨 &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://inlaylab.github.io/Opaline/playground/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Playground&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: type your own name. Every setting lives in the URL, so you can share an exact avatar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⭐ &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/Inlaylab/Opaline" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: MIT for code and art.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;code&gt;npm i @inlaylab/opaline&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One question I'd really like your take on: &lt;strong&gt;is "byte-identical within a major version" the right contract?&lt;/strong&gt; Or would you rather have "looks the same" and let me fix rendering details in minor releases? I went with bytes because it makes CDN caching and email trivially safe, but it does make every bug fix a judgement call.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your site has a dark mode. Then a client asks, "Can we also have a blue theme? And a green one? Oh, and red!" 😅&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suddenly you are staring at &lt;code&gt;dark:bg-gray-900 blue:bg-blue-900 green:bg-green-900 red:bg-red-900&lt;/code&gt; on every element. That is a lot of repeated classes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is a cleaner way. You define every theme's colors &lt;strong&gt;once&lt;/strong&gt; in your global CSS. To switch themes, you change &lt;strong&gt;one class&lt;/strong&gt; on the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; element. No page refresh, no HTML changes, no per-element theme classes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ready to see how it works? 🚀&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What Is a Multi-Theme System in Next.js?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A multi-theme system lets users switch between more than two color schemes, such as light, dark, blue, green, and red. The switch happens instantly, with no reload.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of a &lt;strong&gt;TV remote&lt;/strong&gt;. The TV (your HTML) stays exactly the same. You press a button (change one class) and the colors change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The idea has three parts:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CSS variables&lt;/strong&gt; hold the colors, like &lt;code&gt;--background&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--primary&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, like &lt;code&gt;blue&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;red&lt;/code&gt;, decides which set of values is active.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Your components&lt;/strong&gt; use names like &lt;code&gt;bg-background&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;text-foreground&lt;/code&gt;, never specific colors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your components never know which theme is active. They just ask for "the background color" and the CSS answers.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Why This Topic Matters
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Theming gets messy fast when colors are written directly into components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adding a new theme means editing many files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rebranding means hunting through the whole codebase for color classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Markup gets longer and harder to read.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With the variable approach, a new theme is one new block in one CSS file. Components stay untouched.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Benefits with Real-Life Examples
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clean HTML and JSX.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;className="bg-background text-foreground"&lt;/code&gt; replaces a long chain of per-theme classes. A card component looks the same in every theme.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One place for all colors.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Your client says, "Make the green theme a bit softer." You change one value in &lt;code&gt;globals.css&lt;/code&gt;, and every button, card, and navbar follows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Easy to add new themes.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Want a purple theme? Add a &lt;code&gt;.purple { ... }&lt;/code&gt; block. No component changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instant switching, no refresh.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Changing a class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; makes the browser re-apply styles. There is no page reload, and React does not need to re-render your components just to change colors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Less repeated code.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
You are not generating and shipping theme-specific variants for every element, which keeps your markup and CSS leaner. (It will not magically shrink your app by half, but the duplication really does go away.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Step-by-Step: Build It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This guide assumes the &lt;strong&gt;Next.js App Router&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Tailwind CSS v4&lt;/strong&gt;. A note for Tailwind v3 users appears later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 1: Define Your Themes in &lt;code&gt;globals.css&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;"tailwindcss"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;/* Default (light) theme */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nd"&gt;:root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#111827&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#f3f4f6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#4f46e5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;color-scheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.dark&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#0b0f19&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#e5e7eb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#151b2b&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#818cf8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#0b0f19&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;color-scheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.blue&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#eff6ff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#1e3a8a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#dbeafe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#2563eb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.green&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#f0fdf4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#14532d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#dcfce7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#16a34a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.red&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#fef2f2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#7f1d1d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#fee2e2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#dc2626&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;#ffffff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every theme defines the &lt;strong&gt;same variable names&lt;/strong&gt; with different values. That is the whole trick. 💡&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 2: Connect the Variables to Tailwind
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;inline&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--primary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;--color-primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;var&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;--primary-foreground&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now &lt;code&gt;bg-background&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;text-foreground&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;bg-card&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;bg-primary&lt;/code&gt; work as normal Tailwind classes. They read the live CSS variable, so they follow whichever theme class is active.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 3: Use Semantic Classes in Your Components
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PricingCard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"rounded-xl bg-card p-6 text-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text-xl font-bold"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Pro Plan&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Everything you need to ship faster.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mt-4 rounded-lg bg-primary px-4 py-2 text-primary-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Get Started
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;There are no &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;blue:&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;red:&lt;/code&gt; classes anywhere. This markup works for every theme you will ever add.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 4: Create the Theme Switcher
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// components/theme-switcher.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;blue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;green&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;red&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ThemeSwitcher&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;applyTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;documentElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;remove&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;classList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex gap-2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;THEMES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;applyTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"rounded-md bg-primary px-3 py-1 text-sm capitalize text-primary-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Clicking a button removes the old theme class and adds the new one. The colors change instantly. The choice is saved in &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; so it survives a reload.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Step 5: Avoid the "Flash of Wrong Theme"
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You have probably seen this: the page loads white, then flips to dark a moment later. It happens because the saved theme is applied only after React loads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is a tiny inline script that runs &lt;strong&gt;before the page paints&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/layout.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;RootLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;script&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;__html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`
try {
var t = localStorage.getItem('theme');
if (t) document.documentElement.classList.add(t);
} catch (e) {}
`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"bg-background text-foreground"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; is needed because the script changes the &lt;code&gt;class&lt;/code&gt; before React hydrates. Without it, React may warn about a mismatch.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Comparison: Per-Element Theme Classes vs CSS Variables
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Per-element classes (&lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;red:&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;CSS variables + one class&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Markup length&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Grows with every theme&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stays the same&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Adding a new theme&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Edit many components&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Add one CSS block&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Changing a color&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Search across files&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Edit one value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Best for&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Quick one-off tweaks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Real multi-theme apps&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Per-element classes are not "wrong". For a simple light/dark site they work fine. But once you go beyond two themes, variables win on maintainability.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Best Tips and Do's &amp;amp; Don'ts
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do ✅&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;strong&gt;semantic names&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;background&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;primary&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;card&lt;/code&gt;) instead of color names (&lt;code&gt;blue-500&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define &lt;strong&gt;the same set of variables in every theme&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set &lt;code&gt;color-scheme&lt;/code&gt; for dark themes so native elements like scrollbars and form inputs match.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test text contrast in every theme. A readable blue theme can still hide text in the red one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Don't ❌&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't put theme-specific colors directly in components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't forget the pre-paint script, or users will see a flash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don't skip &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; if you use that script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tailwind v3 note:&lt;/strong&gt; v3 has no &lt;code&gt;@theme&lt;/code&gt; block. Map the variables in &lt;code&gt;tailwind.config.js&lt;/code&gt; instead, for example &lt;code&gt;background: "var(--background)"&lt;/code&gt;. If you want opacity modifiers like &lt;code&gt;bg-primary/50&lt;/code&gt; in v3, store the variables as RGB channels (like &lt;code&gt;253 110 78&lt;/code&gt;) and use &lt;code&gt;rgb(var(--primary) / &amp;lt;alpha-value&amp;gt;)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefer a library?&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/pacocoursey/next-themes" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;next-themes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; supports custom theme names through its &lt;code&gt;themes&lt;/code&gt; prop and handles storage and the flash problem for you. The CSS-variable idea in this article works the same way with it.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Common Mistakes People Make
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt; plus custom variants for every theme.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
It feels natural because that is how dark mode is usually taught. The fix is to define semantic variables once.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forgetting to remove the old class.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
If you only add &lt;code&gt;red&lt;/code&gt; and never remove &lt;code&gt;blue&lt;/code&gt;, both classes stay on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, and CSS order decides who wins. Always remove the old theme class first.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missing variables in one theme.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
If &lt;code&gt;.green&lt;/code&gt; forgets &lt;code&gt;--card&lt;/code&gt;, it inherits the value from &lt;code&gt;:root&lt;/code&gt;, so you get odd colors. Keep every theme's variable list identical.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reading &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; during server rendering.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; only exists in the browser. Use it inside event handlers, effects, or the inline script, not in server components.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ignoring accessibility.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
A pretty theme with low contrast is a bad theme. Check readability for every one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the recipe again:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define each theme's colors &lt;strong&gt;once&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;code&gt;globals.css&lt;/code&gt; using CSS variables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map those variables to semantic Tailwind colors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use classes like &lt;code&gt;bg-background&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;text-primary&lt;/code&gt; in your components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switch themes by changing &lt;strong&gt;one class&lt;/strong&gt; on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add a tiny pre-paint script so users never see a flash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The result is cleaner JSX, a single place to manage colors, and instant theme switching with no refresh. Adding a new theme becomes a ten-line job. 😊&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If this helped, you can read more practical dev guides at &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://hamidrazadev.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;hamidrazadev.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. Share it with a developer friend who is still typing &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt; on every div 😄, and tell me in the comments which theme you would add first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI chat apps look simple: a prompt box, a streaming response, maybe citations. Under the hood, session management gets messy fast. How do you persist history across refreshes? How much context do you send to the model? What happens when the network hiccups or the user switches devices?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What "session" actually means
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A session isn't just a request/response pair. It covers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversation history: user and assistant messages across turns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Context window: the subset of history you actually send to the model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metadata: user ID, model version, feature flags, experiments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistence: how long sessions live, how they resume, where they're stored&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your UI needs to render history efficiently, stream new messages, handle reconnects and errors, and stay keyboard- and screen-reader-friendly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Core UI pattern: a session chat hook
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Centralizing message state, loading, errors, and basic persistence in a hook keeps components clean. Here's a simplified usage pattern:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useSessionChat&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/app/recipes/session/chat/hooks/use-session-chat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PromptInput&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/ui/composites/prompt-input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ResponseViewer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/components/ui/composites/response-viewer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SessionChatPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sendMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryLastMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSessionChat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;customer-support-session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sendMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex flex-col h-screen"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex-1 overflow-auto p-6 space-y-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text-right&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text-left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;assistant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponseViewer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"inline-block bg-primary-50 rounded-lg px-4 py-2"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mt-4 p-3 rounded-md bg-red-50 text-sm text-red-800 flex items-center justify-between"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;retryLastMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"ml-4 text-xs underline"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Retry
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"border-t p-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;PromptInput&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleSubmit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;disabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;actionButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"send"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The heavy lifting: state management, pending states, basic retries: lives in the hook, not scattered across components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where to store session data
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session data can live in three places, each with trade-offs:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;In-memory (React state):&lt;/strong&gt; fast, lost on refresh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Local storage:&lt;/strong&gt; persists across reloads, single device only&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Backend storage:&lt;/strong&gt; durable and multi-device, requires APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hook stays agnostic about storage. Hydrating from local storage looks like this:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sendMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hydrateFromHistory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSessionChat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`chat:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hydrateFromHistory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;hydrateFromHistory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`chat:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now sessions survive a refresh without any UI changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Managing context windows
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LLM context windows force you to decide how much history to send each turn. Common strategies:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Last N turns:&lt;/strong&gt; send only the most recent messages (fast, simple)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Summarized history:&lt;/strong&gt; compress older messages into a running summary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Segmented sessions:&lt;/strong&gt; split long conversations into chapters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The UI should show the full history even if the model only sees part of it. A last-N strategy in your &lt;code&gt;sendMessage&lt;/code&gt; handler:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;buildModelPayload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ChatMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;MAX_TURNS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;visibleHistory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;MAX_TURNS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;visibleHistory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The UI stays unchanged; only the payload builder shifts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Handling errors and retries gracefully
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Network hiccups and model errors are inevitable. Bad UIs lose the user's message, show generic banners, and offer no retry path. Better pattern:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preserve the user's message in history&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show per-message error states&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allow "Retry" on that specific message
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// inside message rendering&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;assistant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"button"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;retryMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"mt-2 text-xs text-red-700 underline"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Retry this response
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Accessibility in session UIs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session management isn't just data: it's how the experience feels. Screen readers should announce new messages progressively. Keyboard users need to jump to the latest message, re-open prompts, and interact with citations and feedback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Streaming components need proper &lt;code&gt;aria-live&lt;/code&gt; regions, focusable elements for citations and controls, and predictable tab order across messages and input.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResponseViewer&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;streamedContent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"markdown"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;showCitations&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"polite"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-atomic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;You don't have to become an ARIA expert to get a reasonable default.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Multi-session interfaces
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Many apps need multiple concurrent sessions: conversations per project, customer, or case. Pattern:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Left sidebar lists sessions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Right panel shows active session chat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both wired to the same session hook with different &lt;code&gt;sessionId&lt;/code&gt;s
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SessionsLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessions&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useUserSessions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// your data source&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex h-screen"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;aside&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"w-72 border-r bg-secondary-50"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* session list */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"w-full text-left px-4 py-2 hover:bg-secondary-100"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;router&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/sessions/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text-sm font-medium"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text-xs text-secondary-600"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Updated &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;updatedAtRelative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;aside&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex-1"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SessionChatPage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sessionId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;key={sessionId}&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;SessionChatPage&lt;/code&gt; forces a clean remount when switching sessions, avoiding stale state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Session management checklist
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before shipping, verify:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;History&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users see past messages after refresh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Old messages don't break layout on mobile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long histories still feel fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear strategy for what goes to the model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not spamming the entire history on every call&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network errors preserve the user's message&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users can retry specific messages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timeouts and exceptions show clear, actionable errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New messages announced to screen readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keyboard users navigate messages and actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus doesn't jump unexpectedly during streaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-session&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sessions have stable IDs and URLs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switching sessions is fast and predictable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Session titles or metadata make sense to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The last item is a common gotcha: if you derive session titles from the first user message, make sure that title updates when the message edits or deletes, or you'll show stale labels in the sidebar.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a shorter version of a guide I wrote at Frontkit Studio. The &lt;a href="https://thefrontkit.com/blogs/session-management-in-ai-chat-applications?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=syndication" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;full post&lt;/a&gt; has the complete walkthrough.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbgx7pe2loku8clvbie4n.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbgx7pe2loku8clvbie4n.jpg" alt=" " width="800" height="450"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ftj6w92nqsdtjnrkfizqy.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ftj6w92nqsdtjnrkfizqy.jpg" alt=" " width="800" height="450"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fc3g3so1iejwaq8v5dng2.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fc3g3so1iejwaq8v5dng2.png" alt=" " width="800" height="329"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
A support agent can sound attentive while making a customer repeat the same troubleshooting step for the third time. I wanted the system to remember the outcome, not just the conversation—and to make that memory useful on the next ticket.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ResolveIQ is a support workflow built around that distinction. It combines ordinary operational records in PostgreSQL, a language model for drafting replies, and Hindsight for customer-level memory across conversations. The through-line is simple: a proposed fix is not a resolution. We need to know what was tried, whether it worked, and what the next response should avoid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


The system around the conversation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The application has a React and TypeScript frontend, a FastAPI backend, and PostgreSQL records for customers, tickets, conversations, messages, resolution attempts, and escalations. The support agent uses a server-side Groq client to generate a response. Hindsight provides retain, recall, and reflect operations for customer memories.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I keep those responsibilities separate. PostgreSQL owns facts that need explicit structure and predictable updates: the ticket state, the assignment, the message history, and each attempted solution’s outcome. Hindsight owns the customer memory that should inform a future interaction without turning every memory into a hand-maintained relational schema.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each customer gets a distinct Hindsight bank. The service derives its ID from a configured prefix and customer ID:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;bank_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;settings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hindsight_bank_prefix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;-customer-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That boundary matters. A memory about one customer’s billing history should not be available while answering another customer’s ticket. It also gives the application a clear ownership rule: the ticket database is the system of record for workflow; Hindsight is the system used to retain and retrieve useful customer context.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The design uses &lt;a href="https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hindsight, an open-source agent memory system&lt;/a&gt;, through its Python client. Its &lt;a href="https://hindsight.vectorize.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;retain, recall, and reflect documentation&lt;/a&gt; maps cleanly to the lifecycle here: retain an interaction, recall relevant context before drafting, and reflect when a support agent wants a synthesized view of the customer’s history. That is one practical version of &lt;a href="https://vectorize.io/what-is-agent-memory" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;agent memory for applications&lt;/a&gt;: persistence that participates in the next decision, rather than a transcript archive nobody consults.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The important unit is an attempt
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The central design decision was to represent a proposed solution as a resolution attempt with an outcome. The model’s answer alone is not enough. The system records a proposed fix as &lt;code&gt;pending&lt;/code&gt;; a later response can mark that pending attempt &lt;code&gt;failed&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;succeeded&lt;/code&gt;. Human agents can also add and update attempts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That gives the next generation call two useful sources of context. The recent conversation explains what the customer said. The structured attempt list explains what the support process has already tried and whether it worked. Customer memory adds context that may span tickets: for example, recurring account conditions or an earlier resolution worth reusing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The prompt builder puts those sources into distinct sections instead of flattening everything into a vague summary:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;SYSTEM_INSTRUCTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;--- CURRENT CONTEXT ---&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;customer_info&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Customer Memories:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;memories_str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Prior Attempted Solutions on this Ticket (DO NOT REPEAT FAILED ONES):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;attempts_str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is intentionally explicit. A failed password reset and a customer preference are different kinds of information, and they should not be interchangeable just because both appear in prose. Attempts are auditable workflow records. Hindsight memories are retrieved context. The model gets both, with clear instructions about the action it must take.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would not describe this as a mathematical guarantee that a model can never repeat a failed fix. A model can misunderstand context or produce an unexpected response. The engineering goal is narrower and testable: preserve the outcomes, place failed attempts in front of the model, instruct it not to repeat them, and keep the proposed next action visible to support staff. If a hard prohibition is required for a particular class of operation, enforce that in application logic rather than trusting prompt wording.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Retrieve, reason, record
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For each reply, the backend saves the incoming customer message first. It then recalls Hindsight memories using a query formed from the ticket subject and current message. The recalled results and recent conversation are passed to the model. After generation, the backend separates customer-facing text from a metadata block, updates the ticket and attempt records, retains the exchange in Hindsight, and evaluates escalation policies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The memory call is kept out of the event loop’s blocking path. The service wraps the synchronous SDK call with &lt;code&gt;asyncio.to_thread&lt;/code&gt; and updates its status only after a successful call:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;to_thread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;except&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;MemoryNotConfigured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;except&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Exception&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;__name__&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;MemoryServiceError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;exc&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_success_at&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;utcnow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;last_error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;That wrapper gives the API a consistent boundary around configuration and service failures. A missing or unavailable memory service should be observable as such; the application should not quietly pretend that recall happened. In a production deployment, I would pair this boundary with timeouts, retry policy appropriate to the request path, and operational alerts based on memory availability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The streaming path follows the same sequence while emitting status and response deltas over server-sent events. It holds back a short suffix of generated text so a metadata delimiter split across token chunks is not accidentally shown to the customer. Once the model’s metadata block begins, it accumulates that separately. The customer sees the reply as it arrives; the backend still gets structured fields to record the proposed solution, intent, category, and priority.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A concrete interaction
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine a customer whose card keeps failing during checkout. On the first ticket, the agent suggests removing and re-adding the card. The backend stores that proposal as a pending attempt. The customer replies that it did not work, and the next update marks the attempt failed. The exchange is also retained in that customer’s Hindsight bank.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Later, the customer opens a related ticket and says checkout still fails. The agent recalls relevant customer context, reads the new ticket’s attempt history, and gets the failed card re-add step in a dedicated prompt section. Its instructions tell it to propose a fresh alternative, acknowledge the failed step, and avoid claiming it has performed irreversible actions such as issuing a refund or resetting an account. The draft’s proposed fix is recorded as a new pending attempt, ready for an agent or customer outcome to resolve.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This combination is more useful than relying on memory alone. The ticket’s attempt rows provide precise, inspectable outcomes for that issue. Hindsight can surface relevant context across tickets without requiring the application to copy and query every old conversation itself. The model receives a compact working context; the application retains the durable operational facts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If attempts continue to fail, escalation rules can create an internal review record. The policy engine can also flag repeated complaints, unresolved tickets past a configured age, and high-priority issues. The escalation snapshot includes the ticket history, attempts, customer information, and related tickets so a human can pick up the case with context. In a complete deployment, those policies and routing integrations should be backed by operational monitoring and clear ownership; creating a record is only the first step in a reliable handoff.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Separate memory from workflow state
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A semantic memory store is useful for retrieving context, but it should not become the only place that records whether a fix failed. Outcomes need explicit fields, audit history, and predictable updates. Use the memory layer to help find context; use the relational database for decisions the workflow must enforce and explain.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


2. Persist outcomes, not just transcripts
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A long conversation is not a reliable representation of what the support process tried. Explicit resolution attempts make the failure legible to both the next model call and a human agent. If the outcome is unknown, represent it as unknown or pending rather than inferring success from silence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Make memory failures visible
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A system that silently substitutes “no memories” when recall fails is difficult to debug and can produce misleading confidence. Expose whether recall and retain succeeded, track the last successful call and last error, and design the product’s fallback behavior intentionally. Memory is a dependency with failure modes, not a prompt decoration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


4. Keep model output inside application boundaries
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The model can suggest a category, priority, and solution, but the backend validates categories and only allows priority to rise. It records the proposal as pending instead of treating generated text as completed work. That separation is essential whenever a reply can affect customer expectations or downstream operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


5. Use memory to reduce repetition, then verify the result
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recall can help an agent avoid asking the customer to start over. It cannot prove a fix worked. The system still needs a follow-up outcome, whether from the customer or a human agent, before a suggestion becomes a successful resolution. That feedback is what makes the next interaction better grounded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The useful promise of this design is not that a language model will never make a mistake. It is that the support system can remember what it tried, carry the outcome forward, and make the next response answerable to that history. Hindsight supplies the cross-ticket context; explicit attempt records keep the workflow honest. That is the foundation I would want before trusting an AI agent with a customer who has already heard “try it again.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rendering a page should not change anything. &lt;a href="https://nakodo.app/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Nakodo&lt;/a&gt; breaks that rule in five places, and every one of them is on purpose, so I went and wrote down the rule they actually follow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The app runs outreach campaigns for brands: it finds creators or local businesses that fit a brief, writes to them, and hands over the ones that say yes, which is the bit described on &lt;a href="https://nakodo.app/how-it-works" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;how it works&lt;/a&gt;. Every page in this post is behind the login, which turns out to be half the reason the pattern is safe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


One: the first page you load creates your account row
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;requireUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SessionUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/login&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;getProfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;insert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;profiles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onConflictDoNothing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Sign-up creates a profile row. Accounts created any other way, by an operator or at the command line or by a provider that let somebody in through a path we did not build, do not have one, and the first page they load makes it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cost on the ordinary path is zero extra queries, because &lt;code&gt;getProfile&lt;/code&gt; is what the app's layout reads anyway and both functions are wrapped in React's &lt;code&gt;cache&lt;/code&gt;, so the whole thing is one lookup per request however many components ask. The insert is &lt;code&gt;onConflictDoNothing&lt;/code&gt;, so two parallel requests from the same new account produce one row and no error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Two: your billing period rolls forward the first time it is read
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentPeriodStart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;addMonths&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscriptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;currentPeriodStart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;currentPeriodEnd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;subscriptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;returning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Usage limits count from &lt;code&gt;currentPeriodStart&lt;/code&gt;, and on a free plan there is no Stripe webhook to move it. So the period moves when somebody reads it, in a &lt;code&gt;while&lt;/code&gt; loop rather than a single addition, because an account that comes back after four months needs the current window and not the next one after the one it missed. That mechanism has its own post, including what it does about a signup on the 31st.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What matters here is the shape, which is the same as the first one: a predicate that is false in the steady state, and a write that only happens on the edge.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Three: a cut-off research run is put right by the next person who looks at the list
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Research runs inside the request that started it, up to about two minutes of crawling and model calls. If that request dies, the campaign row is left saying &lt;code&gt;researching&lt;/code&gt; and nothing in the system is watching it.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Research cut off mid-run is put right only when the list shows some, so&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// the page doesn't write on every visit.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;some&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;researchIsStale&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;recoverStaleResearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;campaignsNow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;researchIsStale&lt;/code&gt; is a pure function over rows the page has already loaded: status &lt;code&gt;researching&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;updatedAt&lt;/code&gt; more than three minutes ago. Only if one row in the list matches does the write happen at all, and the write is a single statement whose &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; repeats the same conditions, scoped to the signed-in user:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sql&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`case when &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;brief&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is null then 'failed'
when &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;launchedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is not null then 'paused'
else 'draft' end`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;pauseMode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sql&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`case when &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;brief&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is not null and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;launchedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; is not null then 'both' end`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;pauseReason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;researching&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;lt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;updatedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;STALE_RESEARCH_MS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;returning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Three &lt;code&gt;CASE&lt;/code&gt; expressions instead of three round trips, because where the campaign should land depends on what it already had: a campaign with no brief failed, a campaign that was live comes back paused with everything stopped for a person to resume deliberately, and anything else is a draft. Then each recovered campaign refunds the research run it never finished, so a crash does not cost somebody a unit of their plan.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The honest part: &lt;strong&gt;this repair only runs if somebody looks.&lt;/strong&gt; There is no cron sweeping for stale research. An account that starts a campaign, closes the tab at the wrong second and never comes back has a campaign that says &lt;code&gt;researching&lt;/code&gt; until the day it loads a page. For a state that only exists because a request died, and that is only visible on the page that fixes it, I think that is the right trade, and I would not have believed it was deliberate if I had found it without the comment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Four: a page read fetches a logo from somebody else's website, after it has answered
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This one looks worst and I like it most.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;after&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fillLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;after&lt;/code&gt; is Next's post-response hook: the callback runs once the response has been flushed, so the reader waits for none of it. Inside:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fillLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{...}[])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;logoUrl&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;researching&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;has&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;all&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;todo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;add&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;logo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;findSiteLogo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;domain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;logoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;logo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;isNull&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;campaigns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;logoUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;findingLogos&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Campaigns created before the app kept logos have &lt;code&gt;logoUrl&lt;/code&gt; of &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;, which means "never looked". The first page that would display one goes and looks, which is the only honest way to backfill a column whose value lives on another company's website and that nobody should have to wait for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Four guards, and each one is answering a different "what if":&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;logoUrl === null&lt;/code&gt; is the predicate. The steady state writes nothing, and &lt;code&gt;""&lt;/code&gt; is the marker for "we looked and found nothing", so a brand with no usable icon is asked about once, ever.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;.slice(0, 5)&lt;/code&gt; bounds the work. A list of twenty campaigns does not fire twenty outbound requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The module-level &lt;code&gt;Set&lt;/code&gt; stops the same render pass and two quick page loads on one instance from doing the same lookup twice. It is per instance, so on a serverless platform it is a hint and not a lock.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; carries &lt;code&gt;isNull(campaigns.logoUrl)&lt;/code&gt; as well, which is the actual lock: whichever instance writes first wins, and the second update touches no rows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The thing I had not thought about until writing this down: the app-router prefetches on hover, so moving your mouse over a campaign link can run the layout, and the layout is the second &lt;code&gt;fillLogos&lt;/code&gt; call site. A prefetch can start a logo lookup. Because the work is idempotent, bounded and once-per-campaign, that is harmless, and if any of those three stopped being true it would be a bug that only ever happened to people who move their mouse.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Five: opening a support thread is what marks it read
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;lines&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;linesOf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Reading it is what clears the mark. Done after the lines are in hand, so a&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// failure here leaves the mark rather than hiding an unread reply.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;markRead&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unread&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;supportTickets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;readAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;eq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;supportTickets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;getThread&lt;/code&gt; has exactly two callers, the page that shows a thread and the action that replies to it, and both pass &lt;code&gt;{ markRead: true }&lt;/code&gt;. The option exists anyway, because the admin panel counts tickets rather than opening them today, and the day an operator view does open one, the mark-read has to be a thing it can decline: an operator reading your ticket must not clear your unread dot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ordering comment is the whole decision. Load the messages first, then clear the mark, so if the query that clears it fails the user sees the messages &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; keeps the unread dot. The other order loses a reply quietly, and the unread state in this app is &lt;code&gt;read_at is null or last_message_at &amp;gt; read_at&lt;/code&gt;, which means "read" is a claim about an instant rather than a boolean, and a wrong claim is permanent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The rule all five follow
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reading them together, there are four properties, and I would now refuse a sixth one that broke any of them:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A predicate that is false on the ordinary visit.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;!profile&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;periodEnd &amp;lt;= now&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;some(isStale)&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;logoUrl === null&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;unread&lt;/code&gt;. If a page writes on every read, it is not a repair, it is an unlogged mutation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Idempotent, and safe when two requests race.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;onConflictDoNothing&lt;/code&gt; on one, the same conditions repeated in the &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; on the other three, a single statement for the fourth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Scoped to the reader.&lt;/strong&gt; Every one of these &lt;code&gt;WHERE&lt;/code&gt; clauses carries the signed-in user's id, so the worst a read can do is repair its own account's rows. None of these paths is reachable without a session: the auth boundary is one allowlist and none of these pages are on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Anything slow goes after the response.&lt;/strong&gt; The only one that touches the network is the only one wrapped in &lt;code&gt;after&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And one property they all lack, which I am leaving alone: none of them writes an audit row. The audit log is for things a person or an operator did, and "the system noticed something was stale" is not one of those. The repair is visible in the row it fixed, and if I needed a trail of repairs I would want it in the run log, not in the log that answers "who changed my account".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Five reads that write, in 72,683 lines. The reason to count them is that each one was obviously correct on the day I wrote it, and the fifth one is only obviously correct because of a comment about the order of two queries.&lt;/p&gt;
